var BIBLE_RKJV = {
"matthew-plain":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The book of the generation of YahuShua HaMashiach, the son of David, the son of Abraham."},{"n":16,"text":"And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born YahuShua, who is called Mashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Mashiach are fourteen generations."},{"n":18,"text":"Now the birth of YahuShua HaMashiach was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost."},{"n":21,"text":"And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name YAHUSHUA: for he shall save his people from their sins."},{"n":25,"text":"And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name YAHUSHUA. "}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Now when YahuShua was born in Bethlehem of Judea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,"},{"n":4,"text":"And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he demanded of them where Mashiach should be born."}],"3":[{"n":13,"text":"Then cometh YahuShua from Galilee to Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him."},{"n":15,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto him, Suffer it to be so now: for thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness. Then he suffered him."},{"n":16,"text":"And YahuShua, when he was baptized, went up straightway out of the water: and, lo, the heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove, and lighting upon him:"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Then was YahuShua led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil."},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God."},{"n":10,"text":"Then saith YahuShua unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve."},{"n":12,"text":"Now when YahuShua had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee;"},{"n":17,"text":"From that time YahuShua began to preach, and to say, Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand."},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua, walking by the sea of Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of sickness and all manner of disease among the people."}],"7":[{"n":28,"text":"And it came to pass, when YahuShua had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at his doctrine:"}],"8":[{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua put forth his hand, and touched him, saying, I will; be thou clean. And immediately his leprosy was cleansed."},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto him, See thou tell no man; but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them."},{"n":5,"text":"And when YahuShua was entered into Capernaum, there came unto him a centurion, beseeching him,"},{"n":7,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto him, I will come and heal him."},{"n":10,"text":"When YahuShua heard it, he marvelled, and said to them that followed, Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel."},{"n":13,"text":"And YahuShua said unto the centurion, Go thy way; and as thou hast believed, so be it done unto thee. And his servant was healed in the selfsame hour."},{"n":14,"text":"And when YahuShua was come into Peter’s house, he saw his wife’s mother laid, and sick of a fever."},{"n":18,"text":"Now when YahuShua saw great multitudes about him, he gave commandment to depart unto the other side."},{"n":20,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto him, The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head."},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua said unto him, Follow me; and let the dead bury their dead."},{"n":29,"text":"And, behold, they cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, YahuShua, thou Son of God? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?"},{"n":34,"text":"And, behold, the whole city came out to meet YahuShua: and when they saw him, they besought him that he would depart out of their coasts. "}],"9":[{"n":2,"text":"And, behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy, lying on a bed: and YahuShua seeing their faith said unto the sick of the palsy; Son, be of good cheer; thy sins be forgiven thee."},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua knowing their thoughts said, Wherefore think ye evil in your hearts?"},{"n":9,"text":"And as YahuShua passed forth from thence, he saw a man, named Matthew, sitting at the receipt of custom: and he saith unto him, Follow me. And he arose, and followed him."},{"n":10,"text":"And it came to pass, as YahuShua sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and sinners came and sat down with him and his disciples."},{"n":12,"text":"But when YahuShua heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick."},{"n":15,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they fast."},{"n":19,"text":"And YahuShua arose, and followed him, and so did his disciples."},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua turned him about, and when he saw her, he said, Daughter, be of good comfort; thy faith hath made thee whole. And the woman was made whole from that hour."},{"n":23,"text":"And when YahuShua came into the ruler’s house, and saw the minstrels and the people making a noise,"},{"n":27,"text":"And when YahuShua departed thence, two blind men followed him, crying, and saying, Thou Son of David, have mercy on us."},{"n":28,"text":"And when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and YahuShua saith unto them, Believe ye that I am able to do this? They said unto him, Yea, Lord."},{"n":30,"text":"And their eyes were opened; and YahuShua straitly charged them, saying, See that no man know it."},{"n":35,"text":"And YahuShua went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among the people."}],"10":[{"n":5,"text":"These twelve YahuShua sent forth, and commanded them, saying, Go not into the way of the Gentiles, and into any city of the Samaritans enter ye not:"}],"11":[{"n":1,"text":"And it came to pass, when YahuShua had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities."},{"n":2,"text":"Now when John had heard in the prison the works of Mashiach, he sent two of his disciples,"},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see:"},{"n":7,"text":"And as they departed, YahuShua began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken with the wind?"},{"n":25,"text":"At that time YahuShua answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes."}],"12":[{"n":1,"text":"At that time YahuShua went on the sabbath day through the corn; and his disciples were an hungred, and began to pluck the ears of corn, and to eat."},{"n":15,"text":"But when YahuShua knew it, he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed him, and he healed them all;"},{"n":25,"text":"And YahuShua knew their thoughts, and said unto them, Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself shall not stand:"}],"13":[{"n":1,"text":"The same day went YahuShua out of the house, and sat by the sea side."},{"n":34,"text":"All these things spake YahuShua unto the multitude in parables; and without a parable spake he not unto them:"},{"n":36,"text":"Then YahuShua sent the multitude away, and went into the house: and his disciples came unto him, saying, Declare unto us the parable of the tares of the field."},{"n":51,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, Have ye understood all these things? They say unto him, Yea, Lord."},{"n":53,"text":"And it came to pass, that when YahuShua had finished these parables, he departed thence."},{"n":57,"text":"And they were offended in him. But YahuShua said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house."}],"14":[{"n":1,"text":"At that time Herod the tetrarch heard of the fame of YahuShua,"},{"n":12,"text":"And his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told YahuShua."},{"n":13,"text":"When YahuShua heard of it, he departed thence by ship into a desert place apart: and when the people had heard thereof, they followed him on foot out of the cities."},{"n":14,"text":"And YahuShua went forth, and saw a great multitude, and was moved with compassion toward them, and he healed their sick."},{"n":16,"text":"But YahuShua said unto them, They need not depart; give ye them to eat."},{"n":22,"text":"And straightway YahuShua constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away."},{"n":25,"text":"And in the fourth watch of the night YahuShua went unto them, walking on the sea."},{"n":27,"text":"But straightway YahuShua spake unto them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid."},{"n":29,"text":"And he said, Come. And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to YahuShua."},{"n":31,"text":"And immediately YahuShua stretched forth his hand, and caught him, and said unto him, O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?"}],"15":[{"n":1,"text":"Then came to YahuShua scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,"},{"n":16,"text":"And YahuShua said, Are ye also yet without understanding?"},{"n":21,"text":"Then YahuShua went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon."},{"n":28,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour."},{"n":29,"text":"And YahuShua departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there."},{"n":30,"text":"And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at YahuShua’s feet; and he healed them:"},{"n":32,"text":"Then YahuShua called his disciples unto him, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way."},{"n":34,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes."}],"16":[{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto them, Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees."},{"n":8,"text":"Which when YahuShua perceived, he said unto them, O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?"},{"n":13,"text":"When YahuShua came into the coasts of Cesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying, Whom do men say that I the Son of man am?"},{"n":16,"text":"And Simon Peter answered and said, Thou art HaMashiach, the Son of the living God."},{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto him, Blessed art thou, Simon Bar–jona: for flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven."},{"n":20,"text":"Then charged he his disciples that they should tell no man that he was YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"From that time forth began YahuShua to shew unto his disciples, how that he must go unto Jerusalem, and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and be raised again the third day."},{"n":24,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me."}],"17":[{"n":1,"text":"And after six days YahuShua taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart,"},{"n":4,"text":"Then answered Peter, and said unto YahuShua, Lord, it is good for us to be here: if thou wilt, let us make here three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias."},{"n":7,"text":"And YahuShua came and touched them, and said, Arise, and be not afraid."},{"n":8,"text":"And when they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no man, save YahuShua only."},{"n":9,"text":"And as they came down from the mountain, YahuShua charged them, saying, Tell the vision to no man, until the Son of man be risen again from the dead."},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things."},{"n":17,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him hither to me."},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua rebuked the devil; and he departed out of him: and the child was cured from that very hour."},{"n":19,"text":"Then came the disciples to YahuShua apart, and said, Why could not we cast him out?"},{"n":20,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you."},{"n":22,"text":"And while they abode in Galilee, YahuShua said unto them, The Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of men:"},{"n":25,"text":"He saith, Yes. And when he was come into the house, YahuShua prevented him, saying, What thinkest thou, Simon? of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute? of their own children, or of strangers?"},{"n":26,"text":"Peter saith unto him, Of strangers. YahuShua saith unto him, Then are the children free."}],"18":[{"n":1,"text":"At the same time came the disciples unto YahuShua, saying, Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?"},{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua called a little child unto him, and set him in the midst of them,"},{"n":22,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven."}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"And it came to pass, that when YahuShua had finished these sayings, he departed from Galilee, and came into the coasts of Judea beyond Jordan;"},{"n":14,"text":"But YahuShua said, Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven."},{"n":18,"text":"He saith unto him, Which? YahuShua said, Thou shalt do no murder, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness,"},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, If thou wilt be perfect, go and sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come and follow me."},{"n":23,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto his disciples, Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven."},{"n":26,"text":"But YahuShua beheld them, and said unto them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible."},{"n":28,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of man shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel."}],"20":[{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua going up to Jerusalem took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said unto them,"},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said, Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with? They say unto him, We are able."},{"n":25,"text":"But YahuShua called them unto him, and said, Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are great exercise authority upon them."},{"n":30,"text":"And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that YahuShua passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou Son of David."},{"n":32,"text":"And YahuShua stood still, and called them, and said, What will ye that I shall do unto you?"},{"n":34,"text":"So YahuShua had compassion on them, and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed him. "}],"21":[{"n":1,"text":"And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then sent YahuShua two disciples,"},{"n":6,"text":"And the disciples went, and did as YahuShua commanded them,"},{"n":11,"text":"And the multitude said, This is YahuShua the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee."},{"n":12,"text":"And YahuShua went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves,"},{"n":16,"text":"And said unto him, Hearest thou what these say? And YahuShua saith unto them, Yea; have ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise?"},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do this which is done to the fig tree, but also if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; it shall be done."},{"n":24,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, I also will ask you one thing, which if ye tell me, I in like wise will tell you by what authority I do these things."},{"n":27,"text":"And they answered YahuShua, and said, We cannot tell. And he said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things."},{"n":31,"text":"Whether of them twain did the will of his father? They say unto him, The first. YahuShua saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, That the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you."},{"n":42,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner: this is the Lord’s doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?"}],"22":[{"n":1,"text":"And YahuShua answered and spake unto them again by parables, and said,"},{"n":18,"text":"But YahuShua perceived their wickedness, and said, Why tempt ye me, ye hypocrites?"},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God."},{"n":37,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind."},{"n":41,"text":"While the Pharisees were gathered together, YahuShua asked them,"},{"n":42,"text":"Saying, What think ye of Mashiach? whose son is he? They say unto him, The Son of David."}],"23":[{"n":1,"text":"Then spake YahuShua to the multitude, and to his disciples,"},{"n":8,"text":"But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your Master, even Mashiach; and all ye are brethren."},{"n":10,"text":"Neither be ye called masters: for one is your Master, even Mashiach."}],"24":[{"n":1,"text":"And YahuShua went out, and departed from the temple: and his disciples came to him for to shew him the buildings of the temple."},{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down."},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, Take heed that no man deceive you."},{"n":5,"text":"For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Mashiach; and shall deceive many."},{"n":23,"text":"Then if any man shall say unto you, Lo, here is Mashiach, or there; believe it not."},{"n":24,"text":"For there shall arise false Messiahs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect."}],"26":[{"n":1,"text":"And it came to pass, when YahuShua had finished all these sayings, he said unto his disciples,"},{"n":4,"text":"And consulted that they might take YahuShua by subtilty, and kill him. "},{"n":6,"text":"Now when YahuShua was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,"},{"n":10,"text":"When YahuShua understood it, he said unto them, Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me."},{"n":17,"text":"Now the first day of the feast of unleavened bread the disciples came to YahuShua, saying unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?"},{"n":19,"text":"And the disciples did as YahuShua had appointed them; and they made ready the passover."},{"n":26,"text":"And as they were eating, YahuShua took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body."},{"n":31,"text":"Then saith YahuShua unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad."},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice."},{"n":36,"text":"Then cometh YahuShua with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder."},{"n":49,"text":"And forthwith he came to YahuShua, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him."},{"n":50,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Friend, wherefore art thou come? Then came they, and laid hands on YahuShua, and took him."},{"n":51,"text":"And, behold, one of them which were with YahuShua stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest’s, and smote off his ear."},{"n":52,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto him, Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword."},{"n":55,"text":"In that same hour said YahuShua to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me? I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me."},{"n":57,"text":"And they that had laid hold on YahuShua led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled."},{"n":59,"text":"Now the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against YahuShua, to put him to death;"},{"n":63,"text":"But YahuShua held his peace. And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be HaMashiach, the Son of God."},{"n":64,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven."},{"n":68,"text":"Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Mashiach, Who is he that smote thee?"},{"n":69,"text":"Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with YahuShua of Galilee."},{"n":71,"text":"And when he was gone out into the porch, another maid saw him, and said unto them that were there, This fellow was also with YahuShua of Nazareth."},{"n":75,"text":"And Peter remembered the word of YahuShua, which said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice. And he went out, and wept bitterly. "}],"27":[{"n":1,"text":"When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against YahuShua to put him to death:"},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And YahuShua said unto him, Thou sayest."},{"n":17,"text":"Therefore when they were gathered together, Pilate said unto them, Whom will ye that I release unto you? Barabbas, or YahuShua which is called Mashiach?"},{"n":20,"text":"But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas, and destroy YahuShua."},{"n":22,"text":"Pilate saith unto them, What shall I do then with YahuShua which is called Mashiach? They all say unto him, Let him be crucified."},{"n":26,"text":"Then released he Barabbas unto them: and when he had scourged YahuShua, he delivered him to be crucified."},{"n":27,"text":"Then the soldiers of the governor took YahuShua into the common hall, and gathered unto him the whole band of soldiers. "},{"n":37,"text":"And set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS YAHUSHUA THE KING OF THE JEWS."},{"n":46,"text":"And about the ninth hour YahuShua cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?"},{"n":50,"text":"YahuShua, when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost."},{"n":54,"text":"Now when the centurion, and they that were with him, watching YahuShua, saw the earthquake, and those things that were done, they feared greatly, saying, Truly this was the Son of God."},{"n":55,"text":"And many women were there beholding afar off, which followed YahuShua from Galilee, ministering unto him:"},{"n":57,"text":"When the even was come, there came a rich man of Arimathea, named Joseph, who also himself was YahuShua’s disciple:"},{"n":58,"text":"He went to Pilate, and begged the body of YahuShua. Then Pilate commanded the body to be delivered."}],"28":[{"n":5,"text":"And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek YahuShua, which was crucified."},{"n":9,"text":"And as they went to tell his disciples, behold, YahuShua met them, saying, All hail. And they came and held him by the feet, and worshipped him."},{"n":10,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them, Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see me."},{"n":16,"text":"Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, into a mountain where YahuShua had appointed them."},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth."}]},
"mark":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The beginning of the gospel of YahuShua HaMashiach, the Son of God;"},{"n":9,"text":"And it came to pass in those days, that YahuShua came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized of John in Jordan."},{"n":14,"text":"Now after that John was put in prison, YahuShua came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God,"},{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men."},{"n":24,"text":"Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou YahuShua of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God."},{"n":25,"text":"And YahuShua rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him."},{"n":41,"text":"And YahuShua, moved with compassion, put forth his hand, and touched him, and saith unto him, I will; be thou clean."},{"n":45,"text":"But he went out, and began to publish it much, and to blaze abroad the matter, insomuch that YahuShua could no more openly enter into the city, but was without in desert places: and they came to him from every quarter. "}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"When YahuShua saw their faith, he said unto the sick of the palsy, Son, thy sins be forgiven thee."},{"n":8,"text":"And immediately when YahuShua perceived in his spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, he said unto them, Why reason ye these things in your hearts?"},{"n":15,"text":"And it came to pass, that, as YahuShua sat at meat in his house, many publicans and sinners sat also together with YahuShua and his disciples: for there were many, and they followed him."},{"n":17,"text":"When YahuShua heard it, he saith unto them, They that are whole have no need of the physician, but they that are sick: I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance."},{"n":19,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber fast, while the bridegroom is with them? as long as they have the bridegroom with them, they cannot fast."}],"3":[{"n":7,"text":"But YahuShua withdrew himself with his disciples to the sea: and a great multitude from Galilee followed him, and from Judea,"}],"5":[{"n":6,"text":"But when he saw YahuShua afar off, he ran and worshipped him,"},{"n":7,"text":"And cried with a loud voice, and said, What have I to do with thee, YahuShua, thou Son of the most high God? I adjure thee by God, that thou torment me not."},{"n":13,"text":"And forthwith YahuShua gave them leave. And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea, (they were about two thousand;) and were choked in the sea."},{"n":15,"text":"And they come to YahuShua, and see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid."},{"n":19,"text":"Howbeit YahuShua suffered him not, but saith unto him, Go home to thy friends, and tell them how great things the Lord hath done for thee, and hath had compassion on thee."},{"n":20,"text":"And he departed, and began to publish in Decapolis how great things YahuShua had done for him: and all men did marvel."},{"n":21,"text":"And when YahuShua was passed over again by ship unto the other side, much people gathered unto him: and he was nigh unto the sea."},{"n":24,"text":"And YahuShua went with him; and much people followed him, and thronged him."},{"n":27,"text":"When she had heard of YahuShua, came in the press behind, and touched his garment."},{"n":30,"text":"And YahuShua, immediately knowing in himself that virtue had gone out of him, turned him about in the press, and said, Who touched my clothes?"},{"n":36,"text":"As soon as YahuShua heard the word that was spoken, he saith unto the ruler of the synagogue, Be not afraid, only believe."}],"6":[{"n":4,"text":"But YahuShua said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, but in his own country, and among his own kin, and in his own house."},{"n":30,"text":"And the apostles gathered themselves together unto YahuShua, and told him all things, both what they had done, and what they had taught."},{"n":34,"text":"And YahuShua, when he came out, saw much people, and was moved with compassion toward them, because they were as sheep not having a shepherd: and he began to teach them many things."}],"7":[{"n":27,"text":"But YahuShua said unto her, Let the children first be filled: for it is not meet to take the children’s bread, and to cast it unto the dogs."}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"In those days the multitude being very great, and having nothing to eat, YahuShua called his disciples unto him, and saith unto them,"},{"n":17,"text":"And when YahuShua knew it, he saith unto them, Why reason ye, because ye have no bread? perceive ye not yet, neither understand? have ye your heart yet hardened?"},{"n":27,"text":"And YahuShua went out, and his disciples, into the towns of Cesarea Philippi: and by the way he asked his disciples, saying unto them, Whom do men say that I am?"},{"n":29,"text":"And he saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am? And Peter answereth and saith unto him, Thou art HaMashiach."}],"9":[{"n":2,"text":"And after six days YahuShua taketh with him Peter, and James, and John, and leadeth them up into an high mountain apart by themselves: and he was transfigured before them."},{"n":4,"text":"And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses: and they were talking with YahuShua."},{"n":5,"text":"And Peter answered and said to YahuShua, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias."},{"n":8,"text":"And suddenly, when they had looked round about, they saw no man any more, save YahuShua only with themselves."},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, If thou canst believe, all things are possible to him that believeth."},{"n":25,"text":"When YahuShua saw that the people came running together, he rebuked the foul spirit, saying unto him, Thou dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee, come out of him, and enter no more into him."},{"n":27,"text":"But YahuShua took him by the hand, and lifted him up; and he arose."},{"n":39,"text":"But YahuShua said, Forbid him not: for there is no man which shall do a miracle in my name, that can lightly speak evil of me."},{"n":41,"text":"For whosoever shall give you a cup of water to drink in my name, because ye belong to Mashiach, verily I say unto you, he shall not lose his reward."}],"10":[{"n":5,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, For the hardness of your heart he wrote you this precept."},{"n":14,"text":"But when YahuShua saw it, he was much displeased, and said unto them, Suffer the little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God."},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God."},{"n":21,"text":"Then YahuShua beholding him loved him, and said unto him, One thing thou lackest: go thy way, sell whatsoever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, take up the cross, and follow me."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua looked round about, and saith unto his disciples, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!"},{"n":24,"text":"And the disciples were astonished at his words. But YahuShua answereth again, and saith unto them, Children, how hard is it for them that trust in riches to enter into the kingdom of God!"},{"n":27,"text":"And YahuShua looking upon them saith, With men it is impossible, but not with God: for with God all things are possible."},{"n":29,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said, Verily I say unto you, There is no man that hath left house, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my sake, and the gospel’s,"},{"n":32,"text":"And they were in the way going up to Jerusalem; and YahuShua went before them: and they were amazed; and as they followed, they were afraid. And he took again the twelve, and began to tell them what things should happen unto him,"},{"n":38,"text":"But YahuShua said unto them, Ye know not what ye ask: can ye drink of the cup that I drink of? and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?"},{"n":39,"text":"And they said unto him, We can. And YahuShua said unto them, Ye shall indeed drink of the cup that I drink of; and with the baptism that I am baptized withal shall ye be baptized:"},{"n":42,"text":"But YahuShua called them to him, and saith unto them, Ye know that they which are accounted to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and their great ones exercise authority upon them."},{"n":47,"text":"And when he heard that it was YahuShua of Nazareth, he began to cry out, and say, YahuShua, thou Son of David, have mercy on me."},{"n":49,"text":"And YahuShua stood still, and commanded him to be called. And they call the blind man, saying unto him, Be of good comfort, rise; he calleth thee."},{"n":50,"text":"And he, casting away his garment, rose, and came to YahuShua."},{"n":51,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto him, What wilt thou that I should do unto thee? The blind man said unto him, Lord, that I might receive my sight."},{"n":52,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole. And immediately he received his sight, and followed YahuShua in the way. "}],"11":[{"n":6,"text":"And they said unto them even as YahuShua had commanded: and they let them go."},{"n":7,"text":"And they brought the colt to YahuShua, and cast their garments on him; and he sat upon him."},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua entered into Jerusalem, and into the temple: and when he had looked round about upon all things, and now the eventide was come, he went out unto Bethany with the twelve."},{"n":14,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto it, No man eat fruit of thee hereafter for ever. And his disciples heard it."},{"n":15,"text":"And they come to Jerusalem: and YahuShua went into the temple, and began to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves;"},{"n":22,"text":"And YahuShua answering saith unto them, Have faith in God."},{"n":29,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, I will also ask of you one question, and answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things."},{"n":33,"text":"And they answered and said unto YahuShua, We cannot tell. And YahuShua answering saith unto them, Neither do I tell you by what authority I do these things. "}],"12":[{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto them, Render to Cesar the things that are Cesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s. And they marvelled at him."},{"n":24,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto them, Do ye not therefore err, because ye know not the scriptures, neither the power of God?"},{"n":29,"text":"And YahuShua answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord:"},{"n":34,"text":"And when YahuShua saw that he answered discreetly, he said unto him, Thou art not far from the kingdom of God. And no man after that durst ask him any question."},{"n":35,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said, while he taught in the temple, How say the scribes that Mashiach is the Son of David?"},{"n":41,"text":"And YahuShua sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury: and many that were rich cast in much."}],"13":[{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto him, Seest thou these great buildings? there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down."},{"n":5,"text":"And YahuShua answering them began to say, Take heed lest any man deceive you:"},{"n":6,"text":"For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Mashiach; and shall deceive many."},{"n":21,"text":"And then if any man shall say to you, Lo, here is Mashiach; or, lo, he is there; believe him not:"},{"n":22,"text":"For false Messiahs and false prophets shall rise, and shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if it were possible, even the elect."}],"14":[{"n":6,"text":"And YahuShua said, Let her alone; why trouble ye her? she hath wrought a good work on me."},{"n":18,"text":"And as they sat and did eat, YahuShua said, Verily I say unto you, One of you which eateth with me shall betray me."},{"n":22,"text":"And as they did eat, YahuShua took bread, and blessed, and brake it, and gave to them, and said, Take, eat: this is my body."},{"n":27,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered."},{"n":30,"text":"And YahuShua saith unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this day, even in this night, before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice."},{"n":48,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto them, Are ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and with staves to take me?"},{"n":53,"text":"And they led YahuShua away to the high priest: and with him were assembled all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes."},{"n":55,"text":"And the chief priests and all the council sought for witness against YahuShua to put him to death; and found none."},{"n":60,"text":"And the high priest stood up in the midst, and asked YahuShua, saying, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?"},{"n":61,"text":"But he held his peace, and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked him, and said unto him, Art thou HaMashiach, the Son of the Blessed?"},{"n":62,"text":"And YahuShua said, I am: and ye shall see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven."},{"n":67,"text":"And when she saw Peter warming himself, she looked upon him, and said, And thou also wast with YahuShua of Nazareth."},{"n":72,"text":"And the second time the cock crew. And Peter called to mind the word that YahuShua said unto him, Before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice. And when he thought thereon, he wept. "}],"15":[{"n":1,"text":"And straightway in the morning the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council, and bound YahuShua, and carried him away, and delivered him to Pilate."},{"n":5,"text":"But YahuShua yet answered nothing; so that Pilate marvelled."},{"n":15,"text":"And so Pilate, willing to content the people, released Barabbas unto them, and delivered YahuShua, when he had scourged him, to be crucified."},{"n":32,"text":"Let Mashiach the King of Israel descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with him reviled him."},{"n":34,"text":"And at the ninth hour YahuShua cried with a loud voice, saying, Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani? which is, being interpreted, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?"},{"n":37,"text":"And YahuShua cried with a loud voice, and gave up the ghost."},{"n":43,"text":"Joseph of Arimathea, an honourable counsellor, which also waited for the kingdom of God, came, and went in boldly unto Pilate, and craved the body of YahuShua."}],"16":[{"n":6,"text":"And he saith unto them, Be not affrighted: Ye seek YahuShua of Nazareth, which was crucified: he is risen; he is not here: behold the place where they laid him."},{"n":9,"text":"Now when YahuShua was risen early the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom he had cast seven devils."}]},
"luke":{"1":[{"n":31,"text":"And, behold, thou shalt conceive in thy womb, and bring forth a son, and shalt call his name YAHUSHUA."}],"2":[{"n":11,"text":"For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Mashiach the Lord."},{"n":21,"text":"And when eight days were accomplished for the circumcising of the child, his name was called YAHUSHUA, which was so named of the angel before he was conceived in the womb."},{"n":26,"text":"And it was revealed unto him by the Holy Ghost, that he should not see death, before he had seen the Lord’s Mashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"And he came by the Spirit into the temple: and when the parents brought in the child YahuShua, to do for him after the custom of the law,"},{"n":43,"text":"And when they had fulfilled the days, as they returned, the child YahuShua tarried behind in Jerusalem; and Joseph and his mother knew not of it. "},{"n":52,"text":"And YahuShua increased in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and man. "}],"3":[{"n":15,"text":"And as the people were in expectation, and all men mused in their hearts of John, whether he were HaMashiach, or not;"},{"n":21,"text":"Now when all the people were baptized, it came to pass, that YahuShua also being baptized, and praying, the heaven was opened,"},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua himself began to be about thirty years of age, being (as was supposed) the son of Joseph, which was the son of Heli,"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"And YahuShua being full of the Holy Ghost returned from Jordan, and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness,"},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua answered him, saying, It is written, That man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word of God."},{"n":8,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto him, Get thee behind me, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve."},{"n":12,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto him, It is said, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God."},{"n":14,"text":"And YahuShua returned in the power of the Spirit into Galilee: and there went out a fame of him through all the region round about."},{"n":34,"text":"Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou YahuShua of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art; the Holy One of God."},{"n":35,"text":"And YahuShua rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him. And when the devil had thrown him in the midst, he came out of him, and hurt him not."},{"n":41,"text":"And devils also came out of many, crying out, and saying, Thou art Mashiach the Son of God. And he rebuking them suffered them not to speak: for they knew that he was Mashiach."}],"5":[{"n":8,"text":"When Simon Peter saw it, he fell down at YahuShua’s knees, saying, Depart from me; for I am a sinful man, O Lord."},{"n":10,"text":"And so was also James, and John, the sons of Zebedee, which were partners with Simon. And YahuShua said unto Simon, Fear not; from henceforth thou shalt catch men."},{"n":12,"text":"And it came to pass, when he was in a certain city, behold a man full of leprosy: who seeing YahuShua fell on his face, and besought him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean."},{"n":19,"text":"And when they could not find by what way they might bring him in because of the multitude, they went upon the housetop, and let him down through the tiling with his couch into the midst before YahuShua."},{"n":22,"text":"But when YahuShua perceived their thoughts, he answering said unto them, What reason ye in your hearts?"},{"n":31,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto them, They that are whole need not a physician; but they that are sick."}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua answering them said, Have ye not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was an hungred, and they which were with him;"},{"n":9,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them, I will ask you one thing; Is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil? to save life, or to destroy it?"},{"n":11,"text":"And they were filled with madness; and communed one with another what they might do to YahuShua."}],"7":[{"n":3,"text":"And when he heard of YahuShua, he sent unto him the elders of the Jews, beseeching him that he would come and heal his servant."},{"n":4,"text":"And when they came to YahuShua, they besought him instantly, saying, That he was worthy for whom he should do this:"},{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua went with them. And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent friends to him, saying unto him, Lord, trouble not thyself: for I am not worthy that thou shouldest enter under my roof:"},{"n":9,"text":"When YahuShua heard these things, he marvelled at him, and turned him about, and said unto the people that followed him, I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel."},{"n":19,"text":"And John calling unto him two of his disciples sent them to YahuShua, saying, Art thou he that should come? or look we for another?"},{"n":22,"text":"Then YahuShua answering said unto them, Go your way, and tell John what things ye have seen and heard; how that the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, to the poor the gospel is preached."},{"n":37,"text":"And, behold, a woman in the city, which was a sinner, when she knew that YahuShua sat at meat in the Pharisee’s house, brought an alabaster box of ointment,"},{"n":40,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto him, Simon, I have somewhat to say unto thee. And he saith, Master, say on."}],"8":[{"n":28,"text":"When he saw YahuShua, he cried out, and fell down before him, and with a loud voice said, What have I to do with thee, YahuShua, thou Son of God most high? I beseech thee, torment me not."},{"n":30,"text":"And YahuShua asked him, saying, What is thy name? And he said, Legion: because many devils were entered into him."},{"n":35,"text":"Then they went out to see what was done; and came to YahuShua, and found the man, out of whom the devils were departed, sitting at the feet of YahuShua, clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid."},{"n":38,"text":"Now the man out of whom the devils were departed besought him that he might be with him: but YahuShua sent him away, saying,"},{"n":39,"text":"Return to thine own house, and shew how great things God hath done unto thee. And he went his way, and published throughout the whole city how great things YahuShua had done unto him."},{"n":40,"text":"And it came to pass, that, when YahuShua was returned, the people gladly received him: for they were all waiting for him."},{"n":41,"text":"And, behold, there came a man named Jairus, and he was a ruler of the synagogue: and he fell down at YahuShua’s feet, and besought him that he would come into his house:"},{"n":45,"text":"And YahuShua said, Who touched me? When all denied, Peter and they that were with him said, Master, the multitude throng thee and press thee, and sayest thou, Who touched me?"},{"n":46,"text":"And YahuShua said, Somebody hath touched me: for I perceive that virtue is gone out of me."},{"n":50,"text":"But when YahuShua heard it, he answered him, saying, Fear not: believe only, and she shall be made whole."}],"9":[{"n":20,"text":"He said unto them, But whom say ye that I am? Peter answering said, HaMashiach of God."},{"n":33,"text":"And it came to pass, as they departed from him, Peter said unto YahuShua, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias: not knowing what he said."},{"n":36,"text":"And when the voice was past, YahuShua was found alone. And they kept it close, and told no man in those days any of those things which they had seen."},{"n":41,"text":"And YahuShua answering said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you, and suffer you? Bring thy son hither."},{"n":42,"text":"And as he was yet a coming, the devil threw him down, and tare him. And YahuShua rebuked the unclean spirit, and healed the child, and delivered him again to his father."},{"n":43,"text":"And they were all amazed at the mighty power of God. But while they wondered every one at all things which YahuShua did, he said unto his disciples,"},{"n":47,"text":"And YahuShua, perceiving the thought of their heart, took a child, and set him by him,"},{"n":50,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Forbid him not: for he that is not against us is for us."},{"n":58,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Foxes have holes, and birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head."},{"n":60,"text":"YahuShua said unto him, Let the dead bury their dead: but go thou and preach the kingdom of God."},{"n":62,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God. "}],"10":[{"n":21,"text":"In that hour YahuShua rejoiced in spirit, and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes: even so, Father; for so it seemed good in thy sight."},{"n":29,"text":"But he, willing to justify himself, said unto YahuShua, And who is my neighbour?"},{"n":30,"text":"And YahuShua answering said, A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and fell among thieves, which stripped him of his raiment, and wounded him, and departed, leaving him half dead."},{"n":37,"text":"And he said, He that shewed mercy on him. Then said YahuShua unto him, Go, and do thou likewise."},{"n":39,"text":"And she had a sister called Mary, which also sat at YahuShua’s feet, and heard his word."},{"n":41,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said unto her, Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things:"}],"13":[{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto them, Suppose ye that these Galileans were sinners above all the Galileans, because they suffered such things?"},{"n":12,"text":"And when YahuShua saw her, he called her to him, and said unto her, Woman, thou art loosed from thine infirmity."},{"n":14,"text":"And the ruler of the synagogue answered with indignation, because that YahuShua had healed on the sabbath day, and said unto the people, There are six days in which men ought to work: in them therefore come and be healed, and not on the sabbath day."}],"14":[{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua answering spake unto the lawyers and Pharisees, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath day?"}],"17":[{"n":13,"text":"And they lifted up their voices, and said, YahuShua, Master, have mercy on us."},{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua answering said, Were there not ten cleansed? but where are the nine?"}],"18":[{"n":16,"text":"But YahuShua called them unto him, and said, Suffer little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God."},{"n":19,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Why callest thou me good? none is good, save one, that is, God."},{"n":22,"text":"Now when YahuShua heard these things, he said unto him, Yet lackest thou one thing: sell all that thou hast, and distribute unto the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, follow me."},{"n":24,"text":"And when YahuShua saw that he was very sorrowful, he said, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!"},{"n":37,"text":"And they told him, that YahuShua of Nazareth passeth by."},{"n":38,"text":"And he cried, saying, YahuShua, thou Son of David, have mercy on me."},{"n":40,"text":"And YahuShua stood, and commanded him to be brought unto him: and when he was come near, he asked him,"},{"n":42,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Receive thy sight: thy faith hath saved thee."}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"And YahuShua entered and passed through Jericho."},{"n":3,"text":"And he sought to see YahuShua who he was; and could not for the press, because he was little of stature."},{"n":5,"text":"And when YahuShua came to the place, he looked up, and saw him, and said unto him, Zaccheus, make haste, and come down; for to day I must abide at thy house."},{"n":9,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, This day is salvation come to this house, forsomuch as he also is a son of Abraham."},{"n":35,"text":"And they brought him to YahuShua: and they cast their garments upon the colt, and they set YahuShua thereon."}],"20":[{"n":8,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things."},{"n":34,"text":"And YahuShua answering said unto them, The children of this world marry, and are given in marriage:"},{"n":41,"text":"And he said unto them, How say they that Mashiach is David’s son?"}],"21":[{"n":8,"text":"And he said, Take heed that ye be not deceived: for many shall come in my name, saying, I am Mashiach; and the time draweth near: go ye not therefore after them."}],"22":[{"n":47,"text":"And while he yet spake, behold a multitude, and he that was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them, and drew near unto YahuShua to kiss him."},{"n":48,"text":"But YahuShua said unto him, Judas, betrayest thou the Son of man with a kiss?"},{"n":51,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said, Suffer ye thus far. And he touched his ear, and healed him."},{"n":52,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto the chief priests, and captains of the temple, and the elders, which were come to him, Be ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and staves?"},{"n":63,"text":"And the men that held YahuShua mocked him, and smote him. "},{"n":67,"text":"Art thou HaMashiach? tell us. And he said unto them, If I tell you, ye will not believe:"}],"23":[{"n":2,"text":"And they began to accuse him, saying, We found this fellow perverting the nation, and forbidding to give tribute to Cesar, saying that he himself is Mashiach a King."},{"n":8,"text":"And when Herod saw YahuShua, he was exceeding glad: for he was desirous to see him of a long season, because he had heard many things of him; and he hoped to have seen some miracle done by him."},{"n":20,"text":"Pilate therefore, willing to release YahuShua, spake again to them."},{"n":25,"text":"And he released unto them him that for sedition and murder was cast into prison, whom they had desired; but he delivered YahuShua to their will."},{"n":26,"text":"And as they led him away, they laid hold upon one Simon, a Cyrenian, coming out of the country, and on him they laid the cross, that he might bear it after YahuShua."},{"n":28,"text":"But YahuShua turning unto them said, Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not for me, but weep for yourselves, and for your children."},{"n":34,"text":"Then said YahuShua, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do. And they parted his raiment, and cast lots."},{"n":35,"text":"And the people stood beholding. And the rulers also with them derided him, saying, He saved others; let him save himself, if he be Mashiach, the chosen of God."},{"n":39,"text":"And one of the malefactors which were hanged railed on him, saying, If thou be Mashiach, save thyself and us."},{"n":42,"text":"And he said unto YahuShua, Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy kingdom."},{"n":43,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, To day shalt thou be with me in paradise."},{"n":46,"text":"And when YahuShua had cried with a loud voice, he said, Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit: and having said thus, he gave up the ghost."},{"n":52,"text":"This man went unto Pilate, and begged the body of YahuShua."}],"24":[{"n":3,"text":"And they entered in, and found not the body of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":15,"text":"And it came to pass, that, while they communed together and reasoned, YahuShua himself drew near, and went with them."},{"n":19,"text":"And he said unto them, What things? And they said unto him, Concerning YahuShua of Nazareth, which was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people:"},{"n":26,"text":"Ought not Mashiach to have suffered these things, and to enter into his glory?"},{"n":36,"text":"And as they thus spake, YahuShua himself stood in the midst of them, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you."},{"n":46,"text":"And said unto them, Thus it is written, and thus it behoved Mashiach to suffer, and to rise from the dead the third day:"}]},
"john":{"1":[{"n":17,"text":"For the law was given by Moses, but grace and truth came by YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"And he confessed, and denied not; but confessed, I am not HaMashiach."},{"n":25,"text":"And they asked him, and said unto him, Why baptizest thou then, if thou be not that Mashiach, nor Elias, neither that prophet?"},{"n":29,"text":"The next day John seeth YahuShua coming unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world."},{"n":36,"text":"And looking upon YahuShua as he walked, he saith, Behold the Lamb of God!"},{"n":37,"text":"And the two disciples heard him speak, and they followed YahuShua."},{"n":38,"text":"Then YahuShua turned, and saw them following, and saith unto them, What seek ye? They said unto him, Rabbi, (which is to say, being interpreted, Master,) where dwellest thou?"},{"n":41,"text":"He first findeth his own brother Simon, and saith unto him, We have found the Mashiach, which is, being interpreted, the Anointed."},{"n":42,"text":"And he brought him to YahuShua. And when YahuShua beheld him, he said, Thou art Simon the son of Jona: thou shalt be called Cephas, which is by interpretation, A stone."},{"n":43,"text":"The day following YahuShua would go forth into Galilee, and findeth Philip, and saith unto him, Follow me."},{"n":45,"text":"Philip findeth Nathanael, and saith unto him, We have found him, of whom Moses in the law, and the prophets, did write, YahuShua of Nazareth, the son of Joseph."},{"n":47,"text":"YahuShua saw Nathanael coming to him, and saith of him, Behold an Israelite indeed, in whom is no guile!"},{"n":48,"text":"Nathanael saith unto him, Whence knowest thou me? YahuShua answered and said unto him, Before that Philip called thee, when thou wast under the fig tree, I saw thee."},{"n":50,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto him, Because I said unto thee, I saw thee under the fig tree, believest thou? thou shalt see greater things than these."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"And the third day there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee; and the mother of YahuShua was there:"},{"n":2,"text":"And both YahuShua was called, and his disciples, to the marriage."},{"n":3,"text":"And when they wanted wine, the mother of YahuShua saith unto him, They have no wine."},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Woman, what have I to do with thee? mine hour is not yet come."},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, Fill the waterpots with water. And they filled them up to the brim."},{"n":11,"text":"This beginning of miracles did YahuShua in Cana of Galilee, and manifested forth his glory; and his disciples believed on him."},{"n":13,"text":"And the Jews’ passover was at hand, and YahuShua went up to Jerusalem,"},{"n":19,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up."},{"n":22,"text":"When therefore he was risen from the dead, his disciples remembered that he had said this unto them; and they believed the scripture, and the word which YahuShua had said."},{"n":24,"text":"But YahuShua did not commit himself unto them, because he knew all men, "}],"3":[{"n":2,"text":"The same came to YahuShua by night, and said unto him, Rabbi, we know that thou art a teacher come from God: for no man can do these miracles that thou doest, except God be with him."},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God."},{"n":5,"text":"YahuShua answered, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born of water and of the Spirit, he cannot enter into the kingdom of God."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto him, Art thou a master of Israel, and knowest not these things?"},{"n":22,"text":"After these things came YahuShua and his disciples into the land of Judea; and there he tarried with them, and baptized."},{"n":28,"text":"Ye yourselves bear me witness, that I said, I am not HaMashiach, but that I am sent before him."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"When therefore the Lord knew how the Pharisees had heard that YahuShua made and baptized more disciples than John,"},{"n":2,"text":"(Though YahuShua himself baptized not, but his disciples,)"},{"n":6,"text":"Now Jacob’s well was there. YahuShua therefore, being wearied with his journey, sat thus on the well: and it was about the sixth hour."},{"n":7,"text":"There cometh a woman of Samaria to draw water: YahuShua saith unto her, Give me to drink."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto her, If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldest have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water."},{"n":13,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto her, Whosoever drinketh of this water shall thirst again:"},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Go, call thy husband, and come hither."},{"n":17,"text":"The woman answered and said, I have no husband. YahuShua said unto her, Thou hast well said, I have no husband:"},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Woman, believe me, the hour cometh, when ye shall neither in this mountain, nor yet at Jerusalem, worship the Father."},{"n":25,"text":"The woman saith unto him, I know that Mashiach cometh, which is called the Anointed: when he is come, he will tell us all things."},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, I that speak unto thee am he."},{"n":29,"text":"Come, see a man, which told me all things that ever I did: is not this HaMashiach?"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, My meat is to do the will of him that sent me, and to finish his work."},{"n":42,"text":"And said unto the woman, Now we believe, not because of thy saying: for we have heard him ourselves, and know that this is indeed HaMashiach, the Saviour of the world."},{"n":44,"text":"For YahuShua himself testified, that a prophet hath no honour in his own country."},{"n":46,"text":"So YahuShua came again into Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain nobleman, whose son was sick at Capernaum."},{"n":47,"text":"When he heard that YahuShua was come out of Judea into Galilee, he went unto him, and besought him that he would come down, and heal his son: for he was at the point of death."},{"n":48,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto him, Except ye see signs and wonders, ye will not believe."},{"n":50,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, Go thy way; thy son liveth. And the man believed the word that YahuShua had spoken unto him, and he went his way."},{"n":53,"text":"So the father knew that it was at the same hour, in the which YahuShua said unto him, Thy son liveth: and himself believed, and his whole house."},{"n":54,"text":"This is again the second miracle that YahuShua did, when he was come out of Judea into Galilee. "}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"After this there was a feast of the Jews; and YahuShua went up to Jerusalem."},{"n":6,"text":"When YahuShua saw him lie, and knew that he had been now a long time in that case, he saith unto him, Wilt thou be made whole?"},{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, Rise, take up thy bed, and walk."},{"n":13,"text":"And he that was healed wist not who it was: for YahuShua had conveyed himself away, a multitude being in that place."},{"n":14,"text":"Afterward YahuShua findeth him in the temple, and said unto him, Behold, thou art made whole: sin no more, lest a worse thing come unto thee."},{"n":15,"text":"The man departed, and told the Jews that it was YahuShua, which had made him whole."},{"n":16,"text":"And therefore did the Jews persecute YahuShua, and sought to slay him, because he had done these things on the sabbath day."},{"n":17,"text":"But YahuShua answered them, My Father worketh hitherto, and I work."},{"n":19,"text":"Then answered YahuShua and said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, The Son can do nothing of himself, but what he seeth the Father do: for what things soever he doeth, these also doeth the Son likewise."}],"6":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua went over the sea of Galilee, which is the sea of Tiberias."},{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua went up into a mountain, and there he sat with his disciples."},{"n":5,"text":"When YahuShua then lifted up his eyes, and saw a great company come unto him, he saith unto Philip, Whence shall we buy bread, that these may eat?"},{"n":10,"text":"And YahuShua said, Make the men sit down. Now there was much grass in the place. So the men sat down, in number about five thousand."},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua took the loaves; and when he had given thanks, he distributed to the disciples, and the disciples to them that were set down; and likewise of the fishes as much as they would."},{"n":14,"text":"Then those men, when they had seen the miracle that YahuShua did, said, This is of a truth that prophet that should come into the world."},{"n":15,"text":"When YahuShua therefore perceived that they would come and take him by force, to make him a king, he departed again into a mountain himself alone."},{"n":17,"text":"And entered into a ship, and went over the sea toward Capernaum. And it was now dark, and YahuShua was not come to them."},{"n":19,"text":"So when they had rowed about five and twenty or thirty furlongs, they see YahuShua walking on the sea, and drawing nigh unto the ship: and they were afraid."},{"n":22,"text":"The day following, when the people which stood on the other side of the sea saw that there was none other boat there, save that one whereinto his disciples were entered, and that YahuShua went not with his disciples into the boat, but that his disciples were gone away alone;"},{"n":24,"text":"When the people therefore saw that YahuShua was not there, neither his disciples, they also took shipping, and came to Capernaum, seeking for YahuShua."},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua answered them and said, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Ye seek me, not because ye saw the miracles, but because ye did eat of the loaves, and were filled."},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, This is the work of God, that ye believe on him whom he hath sent."},{"n":32,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Moses gave you not that bread from heaven; but my Father giveth you the true bread from heaven."},{"n":35,"text":"And YahuShua said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst."},{"n":42,"text":"And they said, Is not this YahuShua, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? how is it then that he saith, I came down from heaven?"},{"n":43,"text":"YahuShua therefore answered and said unto them, Murmur not among yourselves."},{"n":53,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except ye eat the flesh of the Son of man, and drink his blood, ye have no life in you."},{"n":61,"text":"When YahuShua knew in himself that his disciples murmured at it, he said unto them, Doth this offend you?"},{"n":64,"text":"But there are some of you that believe not. For YahuShua knew from the beginning who they were that believed not, and who should betray him."},{"n":67,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto the twelve, Will ye also go away?"},{"n":69,"text":"And we believe and are sure that thou art that Mashiach, the Son of the living God."},{"n":70,"text":"YahuShua answered them, Have not I chosen you twelve, and one of you is a devil?"}],"7":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Jewry, because the Jews sought to kill him."},{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto them, My time is not yet come: but your time is alway ready."},{"n":14,"text":"Now about the midst of the feast YahuShua went up into the temple, and taught."},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua answered them, and said, My doctrine is not mine, but his that sent me."},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, I have done one work, and ye all marvel."},{"n":26,"text":"But, lo, he speaketh boldly, and they say nothing unto him. Do the rulers know indeed that this is the very Mashiach?"},{"n":27,"text":"Howbeit we know this man whence he is: but when Mashiach cometh, no man knoweth whence he is."},{"n":28,"text":"Then cried YahuShua in the temple as he taught, saying, Ye both know me, and ye know whence I am: and I am not come of myself, but he that sent me is true, whom ye know not."},{"n":31,"text":"And many of the people believed on him, and said, When Mashiach cometh, will he do more miracles than these which this man hath done?"},{"n":33,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them, Yet a little while am I with you, and then I go unto him that sent me."},{"n":37,"text":"In the last day, that great day of the feast, YahuShua stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink."},{"n":39,"text":"(But this spake he of the Spirit, which they that believe on him should receive: for the Holy Ghost was not yet given; because that YahuShua was not yet glorified.)"},{"n":41,"text":"Others said, This is HaMashiach. But some said, Shall Mashiach come out of Galilee?"},{"n":42,"text":"Hath not the scripture said, That Mashiach cometh of the seed of David, and out of the town of Bethlehem, where David was?"},{"n":50,"text":"Nicodemus saith unto them, (he that came to YahuShua by night, being one of them,)"}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"YahuShua went unto the mount of Olives."},{"n":6,"text":"This they said, tempting him, that they might have to accuse him. But YahuShua stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground, as though he heard them not."},{"n":9,"text":"And they which heard it, being convicted by their own conscience, went out one by one, beginning at the eldest, even unto the last: and YahuShua was left alone, and the woman standing in the midst."},{"n":10,"text":"When YahuShua had lifted up himself, and saw none but the woman, he said unto her, Woman, where are those thine accusers? hath no man condemned thee?"},{"n":11,"text":"She said, No man, Lord. And YahuShua said unto her, Neither do I condemn thee: go, and sin no more."},{"n":12,"text":"Then spake YahuShua again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life."},{"n":14,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto them, Though I bear record of myself, yet my record is true: for I know whence I came, and whither I go; but ye cannot tell whence I come, and whither I go."},{"n":19,"text":"Then said they unto him, Where is thy Father? YahuShua answered, Ye neither know me, nor my Father: if ye had known me, ye should have known my Father also."},{"n":20,"text":"These words spake YahuShua in the treasury, as he taught in the temple: and no man laid hands on him; for his hour was not yet come."},{"n":21,"text":"Then said YahuShua again unto them, I go my way, and ye shall seek me, and shall die in your sins: whither I go, ye cannot come."},{"n":25,"text":"Then said they unto him, Who art thou? And YahuShua saith unto them, Even the same that I said unto you from the beginning."},{"n":28,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them, When ye have lifted up the Son of man, then shall ye know that I am he, and that I do nothing of myself; but as my Father hath taught me, I speak these things."},{"n":31,"text":"Then said YahuShua to those Jews which believed on him, If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed;"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whosoever committeth sin is the servant of sin."},{"n":39,"text":"They answered and said unto him, Abraham is our father. YahuShua saith unto them, If ye were Abraham’s children, ye would do the works of Abraham."},{"n":42,"text":"YahuShua said unto them, If God were your Father, ye would love me: for I proceeded forth and came from God; neither came I of myself, but he sent me."},{"n":49,"text":"YahuShua answered, I have not a devil; but I honour my Father, and ye do dishonour me."},{"n":54,"text":"YahuShua answered, If I honour myself, my honour is nothing: it is my Father that honoureth me; of whom ye say, that he is your God:"},{"n":58,"text":"YahuShua said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Before Abraham was, I am."},{"n":59,"text":"Then took they up stones to cast at him: but YahuShua hid himself, and went out of the temple, going through the midst of them, and so passed by. "}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"And as YahuShua passed by, he saw a man which was blind from his birth."},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua answered, Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him."},{"n":11,"text":"He answered and said, A man that is called YahuShua made clay, and anointed mine eyes, and said unto me, Go to the pool of Siloam, and wash: and I went and washed, and I received sight."},{"n":14,"text":"And it was the sabbath day when YahuShua made the clay, and opened his eyes."},{"n":22,"text":"These words spake his parents, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had agreed already, that if any man did confess that he was Mashiach, he should be put out of the synagogue."},{"n":35,"text":"YahuShua heard that they had cast him out; and when he had found him, he said unto him, Dost thou believe on the Son of God?"},{"n":37,"text":"And YahuShua said unto him, Thou hast both seen him, and it is he that talketh with thee."},{"n":39,"text":"And YahuShua said, For judgment I am come into this world, that they which see not might see; and that they which see might be made blind."},{"n":41,"text":"YahuShua said unto them, If ye were blind, ye should have no sin: but now ye say, We see; therefore your sin remaineth. "}],"10":[{"n":6,"text":"This parable spake YahuShua unto them: but they understood not what things they were which he spake unto them."},{"n":7,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them again, Verily, verily, I say unto you, I am the door of the sheep."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua walked in the temple in Solomon’s porch."},{"n":24,"text":"Then came the Jews round about him, and said unto him, How long dost thou make us to doubt? If thou be HaMashiach, tell us plainly."},{"n":25,"text":"YahuShua answered them, I told you, and ye believed not: the works that I do in my Father’s name, they bear witness of me."},{"n":32,"text":"YahuShua answered them, Many good works have I shewed you from my Father; for which of those works do ye stone me?"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered them, Is it not written in your law, I said, Ye are gods?"}],"11":[{"n":4,"text":"When YahuShua heard that, he said, This sickness is not unto death, but for the glory of God, that the Son of God might be glorified thereby."},{"n":5,"text":"Now YahuShua loved Martha, and her sister, and Lazarus."},{"n":9,"text":"YahuShua answered, Are there not twelve hours in the day? If any man walk in the day, he stumbleth not, because he seeth the light of this world."},{"n":13,"text":"Howbeit YahuShua spake of his death: but they thought that he had spoken of taking of rest in sleep."},{"n":14,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto them plainly, Lazarus is dead."},{"n":17,"text":"Then when YahuShua came, he found that he had lain in the grave four days already."},{"n":20,"text":"Then Martha, as soon as she heard that YahuShua was coming, went and met him: but Mary sat still in the house."},{"n":21,"text":"Then said Martha unto YahuShua, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died."},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Thy brother shall rise again."},{"n":25,"text":"YahuShua said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live:"},{"n":27,"text":"She saith unto him, Yea, Lord: I believe that thou art HaMashiach, the Son of God, which should come into the world."},{"n":30,"text":"Now YahuShua was not yet come into the town, but was in that place where Martha met him."},{"n":32,"text":"Then when Mary was come where YahuShua was, and saw him, she fell down at his feet, saying unto him, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died."},{"n":33,"text":"When YahuShua therefore saw her weeping, and the Jews also weeping which came with her, he groaned in the spirit, and was troubled,"},{"n":35,"text":"YahuShua wept."},{"n":38,"text":"YahuShua therefore again groaning in himself cometh to the grave. It was a cave, and a stone lay upon it."},{"n":39,"text":"YahuShua said, Take ye away the stone. Martha, the sister of him that was dead, saith unto him, Lord, by this time he stinketh: for he hath been dead four days."},{"n":40,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Said I not unto thee, that, if thou wouldest believe, thou shouldest see the glory of God?"},{"n":41,"text":"Then they took away the stone from the place where the dead was laid. And YahuShua lifted up his eyes, and said, Father, I thank thee that thou hast heard me."},{"n":44,"text":"And he that was dead came forth, bound hand and foot with graveclothes: and his face was bound about with a napkin. YahuShua saith unto them, Loose him, and let him go."},{"n":45,"text":"Then many of the Jews which came to Mary, and had seen the things which YahuShua did, believed on him."},{"n":46,"text":"But some of them went their ways to the Pharisees, and told them what things YahuShua had done."},{"n":51,"text":"And this spake he not of himself: but being high priest that year, he prophesied that YahuShua should die for that nation;"},{"n":54,"text":"YahuShua therefore walked no more openly among the Jews; but went thence unto a country near to the wilderness, into a city called Ephraim, and there continued with his disciples."},{"n":56,"text":"Then sought they for YahuShua, and spake among themselves, as they stood in the temple, What think ye, that he will not come to the feast?"}],"12":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua six days before the passover came to Bethany, where Lazarus was which had been dead, whom he raised from the dead."},{"n":3,"text":"Then took Mary a pound of ointment of spikenard, very costly, and anointed the feet of YahuShua, and wiped his feet with her hair: and the house was filled with the odour of the ointment."},{"n":7,"text":"Then said YahuShua, Let her alone: against the day of my burying hath she kept this."},{"n":9,"text":"Much people of the Jews therefore knew that he was there: and they came not for YahuShua’s sake only, but that they might see Lazarus also, whom he had raised from the dead."},{"n":11,"text":"Because that by reason of him many of the Jews went away, and believed on YahuShua."},{"n":12,"text":"On the next day much people that were come to the feast, when they heard that YahuShua was coming to Jerusalem,"},{"n":14,"text":"And YahuShua, when he had found a young ass, sat thereon; as it is written,"},{"n":16,"text":"These things understood not his disciples at the first: but when YahuShua was glorified, then remembered they that these things were written of him, and that they had done these things unto him."},{"n":21,"text":"The same came therefore to Philip, which was of Bethsaida of Galilee, and desired him, saying, Sir, we would see YahuShua."},{"n":22,"text":"Philip cometh and telleth Andrew: and again Andrew and Philip tell YahuShua."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua answered them, saying, The hour is come, that the Son of man should be glorified."},{"n":30,"text":"YahuShua answered and said, This voice came not because of me, but for your sakes."},{"n":34,"text":"The people answered him, We have heard out of the law that Mashiach abideth for ever: and how sayest thou, The Son of man must be lifted up? who is this Son of man?"},{"n":35,"text":"Then YahuShua said unto them, Yet a little while is the light with you. Walk while ye have the light, lest darkness come upon you: for he that walketh in darkness knoweth not whither he goeth."},{"n":36,"text":"While ye have light, believe in the light, that ye may be the children of light. These things spake YahuShua, and departed, and did hide himself from them."},{"n":44,"text":"YahuShua cried and said, He that believeth on me, believeth not on me, but on him that sent me."}],"13":[{"n":1,"text":"Now before the feast of the passover, when YahuShua knew that his hour was come that he should depart out of this world unto the Father, having loved his own which were in the world, he loved them unto the end."},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua knowing that the Father had given all things into his hands, and that he was come from God, and went to God;"},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto him, What I do thou knowest not now; but thou shalt know hereafter."},{"n":8,"text":"Peter saith unto him, Thou shalt never wash my feet. YahuShua answered him, If I wash thee not, thou hast no part with me."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua saith to him, He that is washed needeth not save to wash his feet, but is clean every whit: and ye are clean, but not all."},{"n":21,"text":"When YahuShua had thus said, he was troubled in spirit, and testified, and said, Verily, verily, I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me."},{"n":23,"text":"Now there was leaning on YahuShua’s bosom one of his disciples, whom YahuShua loved."},{"n":25,"text":"He then lying on YahuShua’s breast saith unto him, Lord, who is it?"},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua answered, He it is, to whom I shall give a sop, when I have dipped it. And when he had dipped the sop, he gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon."},{"n":27,"text":"And after the sop Satan entered into him. Then said YahuShua unto him, That thou doest, do quickly."},{"n":29,"text":"For some of them thought, because Judas had the bag, that YahuShua had said unto him, Buy those things that we have need of against the feast; or, that he should give something to the poor."},{"n":31,"text":"Therefore, when he was gone out, YahuShua said, Now is the Son of man glorified, and God is glorified in him."},{"n":36,"text":"Simon Peter said unto him, Lord, whither goest thou? YahuShua answered him, Whither I go, thou canst not follow me now; but thou shalt follow me afterwards."},{"n":38,"text":"YahuShua answered him, Wilt thou lay down thy life for my sake? Verily, verily, I say unto thee, The cock shall not crow, till thou hast denied me thrice. "}],"14":[{"n":6,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me."},{"n":9,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, Have I been so long time with you, and yet hast thou not known me, Philip? he that hath seen me hath seen the Father; and how sayest thou then, Shew us the Father?"},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua answered and said unto him, If a man love me, he will keep my words: and my Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and make our abode with him."}],"16":[{"n":19,"text":"Now YahuShua knew that they were desirous to ask him, and said unto them, Do ye enquire among yourselves of that I said, A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me?"},{"n":31,"text":"YahuShua answered them, Do ye now believe?"}],"17":[{"n":1,"text":"These words spake YahuShua, and lifted up his eyes to heaven, and said, Father, the hour is come; glorify thy Son, that thy Son also may glorify thee:"},{"n":3,"text":"And this is life eternal, that they might know thee the only true God, and YahuShua HaMashiach, whom thou hast sent."}],"18":[{"n":1,"text":"When YahuShua had spoken these words, he went forth with his disciples over the brook Cedron, where was a garden, into the which he entered, and his disciples."},{"n":2,"text":"And Judas also, which betrayed him, knew the place: for YahuShua ofttimes resorted thither with his disciples."},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua therefore, knowing all things that should come upon him, went forth, and said unto them, Whom seek ye?"},{"n":5,"text":"They answered him, YahuShua of Nazareth. YahuShua saith unto them, I am he. And Judas also, which betrayed him, stood with them."},{"n":7,"text":"Then asked he them again, Whom seek ye? And they said, YahuShua of Nazareth."},{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua answered, I have told you that I am he: if therefore ye seek me, let these go their way:"},{"n":11,"text":"Then said YahuShua unto Peter, Put up thy sword into the sheath: the cup which my Father hath given me, shall I not drink it?"},{"n":12,"text":"Then the band and the captain and officers of the Jews took YahuShua, and bound him,"},{"n":15,"text":"And Simon Peter followed YahuShua, and so did another disciple: that disciple was known unto the high priest, and went in with YahuShua into the palace of the high priest."},{"n":19,"text":"The high priest then asked YahuShua of his disciples, and of his doctrine."},{"n":20,"text":"YahuShua answered him, I spake openly to the world; I ever taught in the synagogue, and in the temple, whither the Jews always resort; and in secret have I said nothing."},{"n":22,"text":"And when he had thus spoken, one of the officers which stood by struck YahuShua with the palm of his hand, saying, Answerest thou the high priest so?"},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua answered him, If I have spoken evil, bear witness of the evil: but if well, why smitest thou me?"},{"n":28,"text":"Then led they YahuShua from Caiaphas unto the hall of judgment: and it was early; and they themselves went not into the judgment hall, lest they should be defiled; but that they might eat the passover."},{"n":32,"text":"That the saying of YahuShua might be fulfilled, which he spake, signifying what death he should die."},{"n":33,"text":"Then Pilate entered into the judgment hall again, and called YahuShua, and said unto him, Art thou the King of the Jews?"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered him, Sayest thou this thing of thyself, or did others tell it thee of me?"},{"n":36,"text":"YahuShua answered, My kingdom is not of this world: if my kingdom were of this world, then would my servants fight, that I should not be delivered to the Jews: but now is my kingdom not from hence."},{"n":37,"text":"Pilate therefore said unto him, Art thou a king then? YahuShua answered, Thou sayest that I am a king. To this end was I born, and for this cause came I into the world, that I should bear witness unto the truth. Every one that is of the truth heareth my voice."}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"Then Pilate therefore took YahuShua, and scourged him. "},{"n":5,"text":"Then came YahuShua forth, wearing the crown of thorns, and the purple robe. And Pilate saith unto them, Behold the man!"},{"n":9,"text":"And went again into the judgment hall, and saith unto YahuShua, Whence art thou? But YahuShua gave him no answer."},{"n":11,"text":"YahuShua answered, Thou couldest have no power at all against me, except it were given thee from above: therefore he that delivered me unto thee hath the greater sin."},{"n":13,"text":"When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he brought YahuShua forth, and sat down in the judgment seat in a place that is called the Pavement, but in the Hebrew, Gabbatha."},{"n":16,"text":"Then delivered he him therefore unto them to be crucified. And they took YahuShua, and led him away."},{"n":18,"text":"Where they crucified him, and two other with him, on either side one, and YahuShua in the midst."},{"n":19,"text":"And Pilate wrote a title, and put it on the cross. And the writing was, YAHUSHUA OF NAZARETH THE KING OF THE JEWS."},{"n":20,"text":"This title then read many of the Jews: for the place where YahuShua was crucified was nigh to the city: and it was written in Hebrew, and Greek, and Latin."},{"n":23,"text":"Then the soldiers, when they had crucified YahuShua, took his garments, and made four parts, to every soldier a part; and also his coat: now the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout."},{"n":25,"text":"Now there stood by the cross of YahuShua his mother, and his mother’s sister, Mary the wife of Cleophas, and Mary Magdalene."},{"n":26,"text":"When YahuShua therefore saw his mother, and the disciple standing by, whom he loved, he saith unto his mother, Woman, behold thy son!"},{"n":28,"text":"After this, YahuShua knowing that all things were now accomplished, that the scripture might be fulfilled, saith, I thirst."},{"n":30,"text":"When YahuShua therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up the ghost."},{"n":33,"text":"But when they came to YahuShua, and saw that he was dead already, they brake not his legs:"},{"n":38,"text":"And after this Joseph of Arimathea, being a disciple of YahuShua, but secretly for fear of the Jews, besought Pilate that he might take away the body of YahuShua: and Pilate gave him leave. He came therefore, and took the body of YahuShua."},{"n":39,"text":"And there came also Nicodemus, which at the first came to YahuShua by night, and brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about an hundred pound weight. "},{"n":40,"text":"Then took they the body of YahuShua, and wound it in linen clothes with the spices, as the manner of the Jews is to bury."},{"n":42,"text":"There laid they YahuShua therefore because of the Jews’ preparation day; for the sepulchre was nigh at hand. "}],"20":[{"n":2,"text":"Then she runneth, and cometh to Simon Peter, and to the other disciple, whom YahuShua loved, and saith unto them, They have taken away the Lord out of the sepulchre, and we know not where they have laid him."},{"n":12,"text":"And seeth two angels in white sitting, the one at the head, and the other at the feet, where the body of YahuShua had lain."},{"n":14,"text":"And when she had thus said, she turned herself back, and saw YahuShua standing, and knew not that it was YahuShua."},{"n":15,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Woman, why weepest thou? whom seekest thou? She, supposing him to be the gardener, saith unto him, Sir, if thou have borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away."},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Mary. She turned herself, and saith unto him, Rabboni; which is to say, Master."},{"n":17,"text":"YahuShua saith unto her, Touch me not; for I am not yet ascended to my Father: but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father; and to my God, and your God."},{"n":19,"text":"Then the same day at evening, being the first day of the week, when the doors were shut where the disciples were assembled for fear of the Jews, came YahuShua and stood in the midst, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you."},{"n":21,"text":"Then said YahuShua to them again, Peace be unto you: as my Father hath sent me, even so send I you."},{"n":24,"text":"But Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, was not with them when YahuShua came."},{"n":26,"text":"And after eight days again his disciples were within, and Thomas with them: then came YahuShua, the doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, Peace be unto you."},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed."},{"n":30,"text":"And many other signs truly did YahuShua in the presence of his disciples, which are not written in this book:"},{"n":31,"text":"But these are written, that ye might believe that YahuShua is HaMashiach, the Son of God; and that believing ye might have life through his name. "}],"21":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua shewed himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias; and on this wise shewed he himself. "},{"n":4,"text":"But when the morning was now come, YahuShua stood on the shore: but the disciples knew not that it was YahuShua."},{"n":5,"text":"Then YahuShua saith unto them, Children, have ye any meat? They answered him, No."},{"n":7,"text":"Therefore that disciple whom YahuShua loved saith unto Peter, It is the Lord. Now when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he girt his fisher’s coat unto him, (for he was naked,) and did cast himself into the sea."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, Bring of the fish which ye have now caught."},{"n":12,"text":"YahuShua saith unto them, Come and dine. And none of the disciples durst ask him, Who art thou? knowing that it was the Lord."},{"n":13,"text":"YahuShua then cometh, and taketh bread, and giveth them, and fish likewise."},{"n":14,"text":"This is now the third time that YahuShua shewed himself to his disciples, after that he was risen from the dead."},{"n":15,"text":"So when they had dined, YahuShua saith to Simon Peter, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me more than these? He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee. He saith unto him, Feed my lambs."},{"n":17,"text":"He saith unto him the third time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me? Peter was grieved because he said unto him the third time, Lovest thou me? And he said unto him, Lord, thou knowest all things; thou knowest that I love thee. YahuShua saith unto him, Feed my sheep."},{"n":20,"text":"Then Peter, turning about, seeth the disciple whom YahuShua loved following; which also leaned on his breast at supper, and said, Lord, which is he that betrayeth thee?"},{"n":21,"text":"Peter seeing him saith to YahuShua, Lord, and what shall this man do? "},{"n":22,"text":"YahuShua saith unto him, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee? follow thou me."},{"n":23,"text":"Then went this saying abroad among the brethren, that that disciple should not die: yet YahuShua said not unto him, He shall not die; but, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee?"},{"n":25,"text":"And there are also many other things which YahuShua did, the which, if they should be written every one, I suppose that even the world itself could not contain the books that should be written. Amen.  "}]},
"acts":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The former treatise have I made, O Theophilus, of all that YahuShua began both to do and teach,"},{"n":11,"text":"Which also said, Ye men of Galilee, why stand ye gazing up into heaven? this same YahuShua, which is taken up from you into heaven, shall so come in like manner as ye have seen him go into heaven."},{"n":14,"text":"These all continued with one accord in prayer and supplication, with the women, and Mary the mother of YahuShua, and with his brethren."},{"n":16,"text":"Men and brethren, this scripture must needs have been fulfilled, which the Holy Ghost by the mouth of David spake before concerning Judas, which was guide to them that took YahuShua."},{"n":21,"text":"Wherefore of these men which have companied with us all the time that the Lord YahuShua went in and out among us,"}],"2":[{"n":22,"text":"Ye men of Israel, hear these words; YahuShua of Nazareth, a man approved of God among you by miracles and wonders and signs, which God did by him in the midst of you, as ye yourselves also know:"},{"n":30,"text":"Therefore being a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him, that of the fruit of his loins, according to the flesh, he would raise up Mashiach to sit on his throne;"},{"n":31,"text":"He seeing this before spake of the resurrection of Mashiach, that his soul was not left in hell, neither his flesh did see corruption."},{"n":32,"text":"This YahuShua hath God raised up, whereof we all are witnesses."},{"n":36,"text":"Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly, that God hath made that same YahuShua, whom ye have crucified, both Lord and Mashiach."},{"n":38,"text":"Then Peter said unto them, Repent, and be baptized every one of you in the name of YahuShua HaMashiach for the remission of sins, and ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Ghost."}],"3":[{"n":6,"text":"Then Peter said, Silver and gold have I none; but such as I have give I thee: In the name of YahuShua HaMashiach of Nazareth rise up and walk."},{"n":13,"text":"The God of Abraham, and of Isaac, and of Jacob, the God of our fathers, hath glorified his Son YahuShua; whom ye delivered up, and denied him in the presence of Pilate, when he was determined to let him go."},{"n":18,"text":"But those things, which God before had shewed by the mouth of all his prophets, that Mashiach should suffer, he hath so fulfilled."},{"n":20,"text":"And he shall send YahuShua HaMashiach, which before was preached unto you:"},{"n":26,"text":"Unto you first God, having raised up his Son YahuShua, sent him to bless you, in turning away every one of you from his iniquities. "}],"4":[{"n":2,"text":"Being grieved that they taught the people, and preached through YahuShua the resurrection from the dead."},{"n":10,"text":"Be it known unto you all, and to all the people of Israel, that by the name of YahuShua HaMashiach of Nazareth, whom ye crucified, whom God raised from the dead, even by him doth this man stand here before you whole."},{"n":13,"text":"Now when they saw the boldness of Peter and John, and perceived that they were unlearned and ignorant men, they marvelled; and they took knowledge of them, that they had been with YahuShua."},{"n":18,"text":"And they called them, and commanded them not to speak at all nor teach in the name of YahuShua."},{"n":26,"text":"The kings of the earth stood up, and the rulers were gathered together against the Lord, and against his Mashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"For of a truth against thy holy child YahuShua, whom thou hast anointed, both Herod, and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles, and the people of Israel, were gathered together,"},{"n":30,"text":"By stretching forth thine hand to heal; and that signs and wonders may be done by the name of thy holy child YahuShua."},{"n":33,"text":"And with great power gave the apostles witness of the resurrection of the Lord YahuShua: and great grace was upon them all."}],"5":[{"n":30,"text":"The God of our fathers raised up YahuShua, whom ye slew and hanged on a tree."},{"n":40,"text":"And to him they agreed: and when they had called the apostles, and beaten them, they commanded that they should not speak in the name of YahuShua, and let them go."},{"n":42,"text":"And daily in the temple, and in every house, they ceased not to teach and preach YahuShua HaMashiach. "}],"6":[{"n":14,"text":"For we have heard him say, that this YahuShua of Nazareth shall destroy this place, and shall change the customs which Moses delivered us."}],"7":[{"n":45,"text":"Which also our fathers that came after brought in with Joshua into the possession of the Gentiles, whom God drave out before the face of our fathers, unto the days of David;"},{"n":55,"text":"But he, being full of the Holy Ghost, looked up stedfastly into heaven, and saw the glory of God, and YahuShua standing on the right hand of God,"},{"n":59,"text":"And they stoned Stephen, calling upon God, and saying, Lord YahuShua, receive my spirit."}],"8":[{"n":5,"text":"Then Philip went down to the city of Samaria, and preached Mashiach unto them."},{"n":12,"text":"But when they believed Philip preaching the things concerning the kingdom of God, and the name of YahuShua HaMashiach, they were baptized, both men and women."},{"n":16,"text":"(For as yet he was fallen upon none of them: only they were baptized in the name of the Lord YahuShua.)"},{"n":35,"text":"Then Philip opened his mouth, and began at the same scripture, and preached unto him YahuShua."},{"n":37,"text":"And Philip said, If thou believest with all thine heart, thou mayest. And he answered and said, I believe that YahuShua HaMashiach is the Son of God."}],"9":[{"n":5,"text":"And he said, Who art thou, Lord? And the Lord said, I am YahuShua whom thou persecutest: it is hard for thee to kick against the pricks."},{"n":17,"text":"And Ananias went his way, and entered into the house; and putting his hands on him said, Brother Saul, the Lord, even YahuShua, that appeared unto thee in the way as thou camest, hath sent me, that thou mightest receive thy sight, and be filled with the Holy Ghost."},{"n":20,"text":"And straightway he preached Mashiach in the synagogues, that he is the Son of God."},{"n":22,"text":"But Saul increased the more in strength, and confounded the Jews which dwelt at Damascus, proving that this is very Mashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"But Barnabas took him, and brought him to the apostles, and declared unto them how he had seen the Lord in the way, and that he had spoken to him, and how he had preached boldly at Damascus in the name of YahuShua."},{"n":29,"text":"And he spake boldly in the name of the Lord YahuShua, and disputed against the Grecians: but they went about to slay him."},{"n":34,"text":"And Peter said unto him, Eneas, YahuShua HaMashiach maketh thee whole: arise, and make thy bed. And he arose immediately."}],"10":[{"n":36,"text":"The word which God sent unto the children of Israel, preaching peace by YahuShua HaMashiach: (he is Lord of all:)"},{"n":38,"text":"How God anointed YahuShua of Nazareth with the Holy Ghost and with power: who went about doing good, and healing all that were oppressed of the devil; for God was with him."}],"11":[{"n":17,"text":"Forasmuch then as God gave them the like gift as he did unto us, who believed on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach; what was I, that I could withstand God?"},{"n":20,"text":"And some of them were men of Cyprus and Cyrene, which, when they were come to Antioch, spake unto the Grecians, preaching the Lord YahuShua."}],"13":[{"n":23,"text":"Of this man’s seed hath God according to his promise raised unto Israel a Saviour, YahuShua:"},{"n":33,"text":"God hath fulfilled the same unto us their children, in that he hath raised up YahuShua again; as it is also written in the second psalm, Thou art my Son, this day have I begotten thee."}],"15":[{"n":11,"text":"But we believe that through the grace of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach we shall be saved, even as they."},{"n":26,"text":"Men that have hazarded their lives for the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"16":[{"n":18,"text":"And this did she many days. But Paul, being grieved, turned and said to the spirit, I command thee in the name of YahuShua HaMashiach to come out of her. And he came out the same hour."},{"n":31,"text":"And they said, Believe on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house."}],"17":[{"n":3,"text":"Opening and alleging, that Mashiach must needs have suffered, and risen again from the dead; and that this YahuShua, whom I preach unto you, is Mashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"Whom Jason hath received: and these all do contrary to the decrees of Cesar, saying that there is another king, one YahuShua."},{"n":18,"text":"Then certain philosophers of the Epicureans, and of the Stoicks, encountered him. And some said, What will this babbler say? other some, He seemeth to be a setter forth of strange gods: because he preached unto them YahuShua, and the resurrection."}],"18":[{"n":5,"text":"And when Silas and Timotheus were come from Macedonia, Paul was pressed in the spirit, and testified to the Jews that YahuShua was Mashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"For he mightily convinced the Jews, and that publickly, shewing by the scriptures that YahuShua was Mashiach. "}],"19":[{"n":4,"text":"Then said Paul, John verily baptized with the baptism of repentance, saying unto the people, that they should believe on him which should come after him, that is, on YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":5,"text":"When they heard this, they were baptized in the name of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":10,"text":"And this continued by the space of two years; so that all they which dwelt in Asia heard the word of the Lord YahuShua, both Jews and Greeks."},{"n":13,"text":"Then certain of the vagabond Jews, exorcists, took upon them to call over them which had evil spirits the name of the Lord YahuShua, saying, We adjure you by YahuShua whom Paul preacheth."},{"n":15,"text":"And the evil spirit answered and said, YahuShua I know, and Paul I know; but who are ye?"},{"n":17,"text":"And this was known to all the Jews and Greeks also dwelling at Ephesus; and fear fell on them all, and the name of the Lord YahuShua was magnified."}],"20":[{"n":21,"text":"Testifying both to the Jews, and also to the Greeks, repentance toward God, and faith toward our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":24,"text":"But none of these things move me, neither count I my life dear unto myself, so that I might finish my course with joy, and the ministry, which I have received of the Lord YahuShua, to testify the gospel of the grace of God."},{"n":35,"text":"I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord YahuShua, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive."}],"21":[{"n":13,"text":"Then Paul answered, What mean ye to weep and to break mine heart? for I am ready not to be bound only, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord YahuShua."}],"22":[{"n":8,"text":"And I answered, Who art thou, Lord? And he said unto me, I am YahuShua of Nazareth, whom thou persecutest."}],"24":[{"n":24,"text":"And after certain days, when Felix came with his wife Drusilla, which was a Jewess, he sent for Paul, and heard him concerning the faith in Mashiach."}],"25":[{"n":19,"text":"But had certain questions against him of their own superstition, and of one YahuShua, which was dead, whom Paul affirmed to be alive."}],"26":[{"n":9,"text":"I verily thought with myself, that I ought to do many things contrary to the name of YahuShua of Nazareth."},{"n":15,"text":"And I said, Who art thou, Lord? And he said, I am YahuShua whom thou persecutest."},{"n":23,"text":"That Mashiach should suffer, and that he should be the first that should rise from the dead, and should shew light unto the people, and to the Gentiles."}],"28":[{"n":23,"text":"And when they had appointed him a day, there came many to him into his lodging; to whom he expounded and testified the kingdom of God, persuading them concerning YahuShua, both out of the law of Moses, and out of the prophets, from morning till evening."},{"n":31,"text":"Preaching the kingdom of God, and teaching those things which concern the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, with all confidence, no man forbidding him.  "}]},
"romans":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a servant of YahuShua HaMashiach, called to be an apostle, separated unto the gospel of God,"},{"n":3,"text":"Concerning his Son YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, which was made of the seed of David according to the flesh;"},{"n":6,"text":"Among whom are ye also the called of YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":7,"text":"To all that be in Rome, beloved of God, called to be saints: Grace to you and peace from God our Father, and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"First, I thank my God through YahuShua HaMashiach for you all, that your faith is spoken of throughout the whole world."},{"n":16,"text":"For I am not ashamed of the gospel of Mashiach: for it is the power of God unto salvation to every one that believeth; to the Jew first, and also to the Greek."}],"2":[{"n":16,"text":"In the day when God shall judge the secrets of men by YahuShua HaMashiach according to my gospel."}],"3":[{"n":22,"text":"Even the righteousness of God which is by faith of YahuShua HaMashiach unto all and upon all them that believe: for there is no difference:"},{"n":24,"text":"Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":26,"text":"To declare, I say, at this time his righteousness: that he might be just, and the justifier of him which believeth in YahuShua."}],"4":[{"n":24,"text":"But for us also, to whom it shall be imputed, if we believe on him that raised up YahuShua our Lord from the dead;"}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":6,"text":"For when we were yet without strength, in due time Mashiach died for the ungodly."},{"n":8,"text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Mashiach died for us."},{"n":11,"text":"And not only so, but we also joy in God through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, by whom we have now received the atonement."},{"n":15,"text":"But not as the offence, so also is the free gift. For if through the offence of one many be dead, much more the grace of God, and the gift by grace, which is by one man, YahuShua HaMashiach, hath abounded unto many."},{"n":17,"text":"For if by one man’s offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by one, YahuShua HaMashiach.)"},{"n":21,"text":"That as sin hath reigned unto death, even so might grace reign through righteousness unto eternal life by YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord. "}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"Know ye not, that so many of us as were baptized into YahuShua HaMashiach were baptized into his death?"},{"n":4,"text":"Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that like as Mashiach was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life."},{"n":8,"text":"Now if we be dead with Mashiach, we believe that we shall also live with him:"},{"n":9,"text":"Knowing that Mashiach being raised from the dead dieth no more; death hath no more dominion over him."},{"n":11,"text":"Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":23,"text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord. "}],"7":[{"n":4,"text":"Wherefore, my brethren, ye also are become dead to the law by the body of Mashiach; that ye should be married to another, even to him who is raised from the dead, that we should bring forth fruit unto God."},{"n":25,"text":"I thank God through YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord. So then with the mind I myself serve the law of God; but with the flesh the law of sin. "}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in YahuShua HaMashiach, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."},{"n":2,"text":"For the law of the Spirit of life in YahuShua HaMashiach hath made me free from the law of sin and death."},{"n":9,"text":"But ye are not in the flesh, but in the Spirit, if so be that the Spirit of God dwell in you. Now if any man have not the Spirit of Mashiach, he is none of his."},{"n":10,"text":"And if Mashiach be in you, the body is dead because of sin; but the Spirit is life because of righteousness."},{"n":11,"text":"But if the Spirit of him that raised up YahuShua from the dead dwell in you, he that raised up Mashiach from the dead shall also quicken your mortal bodies by his Spirit that dwelleth in you."},{"n":17,"text":"And if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Mashiach; if so be that we suffer with him, that we may be also glorified together."},{"n":34,"text":"Who is he that condemneth? It is Mashiach that died, yea rather, that is risen again, who is even at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us."},{"n":35,"text":"Who shall separate us from the love of Mashiach? shall tribulation, or distress, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword?"},{"n":39,"text":"Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord. "}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"I say the truth in Mashiach, I lie not, my conscience also bearing me witness in the Holy Ghost,"},{"n":3,"text":"For I could wish that myself were accursed from Mashiach for my brethren, my kinsmen according to the flesh:"},{"n":5,"text":"Whose are the fathers, and of whom as concerning the flesh Mashiach came, who is over all, God blessed for ever. Amen."}],"10":[{"n":4,"text":"For Mashiach is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth."},{"n":6,"text":"But the righteousness which is of faith speaketh on this wise, Say not in thine heart, Who shall ascend into heaven? (that is, to bring Mashiach down from above:)"},{"n":7,"text":"Or, Who shall descend into the deep? (that is, to bring up Mashiach again from the dead.)"},{"n":9,"text":"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord YahuShua, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved."}],"12":[{"n":5,"text":"So we, being many, are one body in Mashiach, and every one members one of another."}],"13":[{"n":14,"text":"But put ye on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and make not provision for the flesh, to fulfil the lusts thereof. "}],"14":[{"n":9,"text":"For to this end Mashiach both died, and rose, and revived, that he might be Lord both of the dead and living."},{"n":10,"text":"But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at nought thy brother? for we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Mashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"I know, and am persuaded by the Lord YahuShua, that there is nothing unclean of itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him it is unclean."},{"n":15,"text":"But if thy brother be grieved with thy meat, now walkest thou not charitably. Destroy not him with thy meat, for whom Mashiach died."},{"n":18,"text":"For he that in these things serveth Mashiach is acceptable to God, and approved of men."}],"15":[{"n":3,"text":"For even Mashiach pleased not himself; but, as it is written, The reproaches of them that reproached thee fell on me."},{"n":5,"text":"Now the God of patience and consolation grant you to be likeminded one toward another according to YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":6,"text":"That ye may with one mind and one mouth glorify God, even the Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"Wherefore receive ye one another, as Mashiach also received us to the glory of God."},{"n":8,"text":"Now I say that YahuShua HaMashiach was a minister of the circumcision for the truth of God, to confirm the promises made unto the fathers:"},{"n":16,"text":"That I should be the minister of YahuShua HaMashiach to the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of God, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be acceptable, being sanctified by the Holy Ghost."},{"n":17,"text":"I have therefore whereof I may glory through YahuShua HaMashiach in those things which pertain to God."},{"n":18,"text":"For I will not dare to speak of any of those things which Mashiach hath not wrought by me, to make the Gentiles obedient, by word and deed,"},{"n":19,"text":"Through mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of God; so that from Jerusalem, and round about unto Illyricum, I have fully preached the gospel of Mashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"Yea, so have I strived to preach the gospel, not where Mashiach was named, lest I should build upon another man’s foundation:"},{"n":29,"text":"And I am sure that, when I come unto you, I shall come in the fulness of the blessing of the gospel of Mashiach."},{"n":30,"text":"Now I beseech you, brethren, for the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach’s sake, and for the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with me in your prayers to God for me;"}],"16":[{"n":3,"text":"Greet Priscilla and Aquila my helpers in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":5,"text":"Likewise greet the church that is in their house. Salute my wellbeloved Epenetus, who is the firstfruits of Achaia unto Mashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"Salute Andronicus and Junia, my kinsmen, and my fellowprisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also were in Mashiach before me."},{"n":9,"text":"Salute Urbane, our helper in Mashiach, and Stachys my beloved."},{"n":10,"text":"Salute Apelles approved in Mashiach. Salute them which are of Aristobulus’ household. "},{"n":16,"text":"Salute one another with an holy kiss. The churches of Mashiach salute you."},{"n":18,"text":"For they that are such serve not our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, but their own belly; and by good words and fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple."},{"n":20,"text":"And the God of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you. Amen."},{"n":24,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen."},{"n":25,"text":"Now to him that is of power to stablish you according to my gospel, and the preaching of YahuShua HaMashiach, according to the revelation of the mystery, which was kept secret since the world began,"},{"n":27,"text":"To God only wise, be glory through YahuShua HaMashiach for ever. Amen.  Written to the Romans from Corinthus, and sent by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea. "}]},
"1corinthians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, called to be an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach through the will of God, and Sosthenes our brother,"},{"n":2,"text":"Unto the church of God which is at Corinth, to them that are sanctified in YahuShua HaMashiach, called to be saints, with all that in every place call upon the name of YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, both theirs and ours:"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":4,"text":"I thank my God always on your behalf, for the grace of God which is given you by YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":6,"text":"Even as the testimony of Mashiach was confirmed in you:"},{"n":7,"text":"So that ye come behind in no gift; waiting for the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":8,"text":"Who shall also confirm you unto the end, that ye may be blameless in the day of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":9,"text":"God is faithful, by whom ye were called unto the fellowship of his Son YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":10,"text":"Now I beseech you, brethren, by the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that ye all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you; but that ye be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment."},{"n":12,"text":"Now this I say, that every one of you saith, I am of Paul; and I of Apollos; and I of Cephas; and I of Mashiach."},{"n":13,"text":"Is Mashiach divided? was Paul crucified for you? or were ye baptized in the name of Paul?"},{"n":17,"text":"For Mashiach sent me not to baptize, but to preach the gospel: not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of Mashiach should be made of none effect."},{"n":23,"text":"But we preach Mashiach crucified, unto the Jews a stumblingblock, and unto the Greeks foolishness;"},{"n":24,"text":"But unto them which are called, both Jews and Greeks, Mashiach the power of God, and the wisdom of God."},{"n":30,"text":"But of him are ye in YahuShua HaMashiach, who of God is made unto us wisdom, and righteousness, and sanctification, and redemption:"}],"2":[{"n":2,"text":"For I determined not to know any thing among you, save YahuShua HaMashiach, and him crucified."},{"n":16,"text":"For who hath known the mind of the Lord, that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Mashiach. "}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"And I, brethren, could not speak unto you as unto spiritual, but as unto carnal, even as unto babes in Mashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":23,"text":"And ye are Mashiach’s; and Mashiach is God’s. "}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Let a man so account of us, as of the ministers of Mashiach, and stewards of the mysteries of God."},{"n":10,"text":"We are fools for Mashiach’s sake, but ye are wise in Mashiach; we are weak, but ye are strong; ye are honourable, but we are despised."},{"n":15,"text":"For though ye have ten thousand instructors in Mashiach, yet have ye not many fathers: for in YahuShua HaMashiach I have begotten you through the gospel."},{"n":17,"text":"For this cause have I sent unto you Timotheus, who is my beloved son, and faithful in the Lord, who shall bring you into remembrance of my ways which be in Mashiach, as I teach every where in every church."}],"5":[{"n":4,"text":"In the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, when ye are gathered together, and my spirit, with the power of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":5,"text":"To deliver such an one unto Satan for the destruction of the flesh, that the spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":7,"text":"Purge out therefore the old leaven, that ye may be a new lump, as ye are unleavened. For even Mashiach our passover is sacrificed for us:"}],"6":[{"n":11,"text":"And such were some of you: but ye are washed, but ye are sanctified, but ye are justified in the name of the Lord YahuShua, and by the Spirit of our God."},{"n":15,"text":"Know ye not that your bodies are the members of Mashiach? shall I then take the members of Mashiach, and make them the members of an harlot? God forbid."}],"7":[{"n":22,"text":"For he that is called in the Lord, being a servant, is the Lord’s freeman: likewise also he that is called, being free, is Mashiach’s servant."}],"8":[{"n":6,"text":"But to us there is but one God, the Father, of whom are all things, and we in him; and one Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, by whom are all things, and we by him."},{"n":11,"text":"And through thy knowledge shall the weak brother perish, for whom Mashiach died?"},{"n":12,"text":"But when ye sin so against the brethren, and wound their weak conscience, ye sin against Mashiach."}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"Am I not an apostle? am I not free? have I not seen YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord? are not ye my work in the Lord?"},{"n":12,"text":"If others be partakers of this power over you, are not we rather? Nevertheless we have not used this power; but suffer all things, lest we should hinder the gospel of Mashiach."},{"n":18,"text":"What is my reward then? Verily that, when I preach the gospel, I may make the gospel of Mashiach without charge, that I abuse not my power in the gospel."},{"n":21,"text":"To them that are without law, as without law, (being not without law to God, but under the law to Mashiach,) that I might gain them that are without law."}],"10":[{"n":4,"text":"And did all drink the same spiritual drink: for they drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them: and that Rock was Mashiach."},{"n":9,"text":"Neither let us tempt Mashiach, as some of them also tempted, and were destroyed of serpents."},{"n":16,"text":"The cup of blessing which we bless, is it not the communion of the blood of Mashiach? The bread which we break, is it not the communion of the body of Mashiach?"}],"11":[{"n":1,"text":"Be ye followers of me, even as I also am of Mashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"But I would have you know, that the head of every man is Mashiach; and the head of the woman is the man; and the head of Mashiach is God."},{"n":23,"text":"For I have received of the Lord that which also I delivered unto you, That the Lord YahuShua the same night in which he was betrayed took bread:"}],"12":[{"n":3,"text":"Wherefore I give you to understand, that no man speaking by the Spirit of God calleth YahuShua accursed: and that no man can say that YahuShua is the Lord, but by the Holy Ghost."},{"n":12,"text":"For as the body is one, and hath many members, and all the members of that one body, being many, are one body: so also is Mashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"Now ye are the body of Mashiach, and members in particular."}],"15":[{"n":3,"text":"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Mashiach died for our sins according to the scriptures;"},{"n":12,"text":"Now if Mashiach be preached that he rose from the dead, how say some among you that there is no resurrection of the dead?"},{"n":13,"text":"But if there be no resurrection of the dead, then is Mashiach not risen:"},{"n":14,"text":"And if Mashiach be not risen, then is our preaching vain, and your faith is also vain."},{"n":15,"text":"Yea, and we are found false witnesses of God; because we have testified of God that he raised up Mashiach: whom he raised not up, if so be that the dead rise not."},{"n":16,"text":"For if the dead rise not, then is not Mashiach raised:"},{"n":17,"text":"And if Mashiach be not raised, your faith is vain; ye are yet in your sins."},{"n":18,"text":"Then they also which are fallen asleep in Mashiach are perished."},{"n":19,"text":"If in this life only we have hope in Mashiach, we are of all men most miserable."},{"n":20,"text":"But now is Mashiach risen from the dead, and become the firstfruits of them that slept."},{"n":22,"text":"For as in Adam all die, even so in Mashiach shall all be made alive."},{"n":23,"text":"But every man in his own order: Mashiach the firstfruits; afterward they that are Mashiach’s at his coming."},{"n":31,"text":"I protest by your rejoicing which I have in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, I die daily."},{"n":57,"text":"But thanks be to God, which giveth us the victory through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"16":[{"n":22,"text":"If any man love not the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, let him be Anathema Maran-atha."},{"n":23,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you."},{"n":24,"text":"My love be with you all in YahuShua HaMashiach. Amen.  The first epistle to the Corinthians was written from Philippi by Stephanas, and Fortunatus, and Achaicus, and Timotheus. "}]},
"2corinthians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, unto the church of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints which are in all Achaia:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace be to you and peace from God our Father, and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be God, even the Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Father of mercies, and the God of all comfort;"},{"n":5,"text":"For as the sufferings of Mashiach abound in us, so our consolation also aboundeth by Mashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"As also ye have acknowledged us in part, that we are your rejoicing, even as ye also are ours in the day of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":19,"text":"For the Son of God, YahuShua HaMashiach, who was preached among you by us, even by me and Silvanus and Timotheus, was not yea and nay, but in him was yea."},{"n":21,"text":"Now he which stablisheth us with you in Mashiach, and hath anointed us, is God;"}],"2":[{"n":10,"text":"To whom ye forgive any thing, I forgive also: for if I forgave any thing, to whom I forgave it, for your sakes forgave I it in the person of Mashiach;"},{"n":12,"text":"Furthermore, when I came to Troas to preach Mashiach’s gospel, and a door was opened unto me of the Lord,"},{"n":14,"text":"Now thanks be unto God, which always causeth us to triumph in Mashiach, and maketh manifest the savour of his knowledge by us in every place."},{"n":15,"text":"For we are unto God a sweet savour of Mashiach, in them that are saved, and in them that perish:"},{"n":17,"text":"For we are not as many, which corrupt the word of God: but as of sincerity, but as of God, in the sight of God speak we in Mashiach. "}],"3":[{"n":3,"text":"Forasmuch as ye are manifestly declared to be the epistle of Mashiach ministered by us, written not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tables of stone, but in fleshy tables of the heart."},{"n":4,"text":"And such trust have we through Mashiach to God-ward:"},{"n":14,"text":"But their minds were blinded: for until this day remaineth the same vail untaken away in the reading of the old testament; which vail is done away in Mashiach."}],"4":[{"n":4,"text":"In whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, lest the light of the glorious gospel of Mashiach, who is the image of God, should shine unto them."},{"n":5,"text":"For we preach not ourselves, but YahuShua HaMashiach the Lord; and ourselves your servants for YahuShua’s sake."},{"n":6,"text":"For God, who commanded the light to shine out of darkness, hath shined in our hearts, to give the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"Always bearing about in the body the dying of the Lord YahuShua, that the life also of YahuShua might be made manifest in our body."},{"n":11,"text":"For we which live are alway delivered unto death for YahuShua’s sake, that the life also of YahuShua might be made manifest in our mortal flesh."},{"n":14,"text":"Knowing that he which raised up the Lord YahuShua shall raise up us also by YahuShua, and shall present us with you."}],"5":[{"n":10,"text":"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Mashiach; that every one may receive the things done in his body, according to that he hath done, whether it be good or bad."},{"n":14,"text":"For the love of Mashiach constraineth us; because we thus judge, that if one died for all, then were all dead:"},{"n":16,"text":"Wherefore henceforth know we no man after the flesh: yea, though we have known Mashiach after the flesh, yet now henceforth know we him no more."},{"n":17,"text":"Therefore if any man be in Mashiach, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new."},{"n":18,"text":"And all things are of God, who hath reconciled us to himself by YahuShua HaMashiach, and hath given to us the ministry of reconciliation;"},{"n":19,"text":"To wit, that God was in Mashiach, reconciling the world unto himself, not imputing their trespasses unto them; and hath committed unto us the word of reconciliation."},{"n":20,"text":"Now then we are ambassadors for Mashiach, as though God did beseech you by us: we pray you in Mashiach’s stead, be ye reconciled to God."}],"6":[{"n":15,"text":"And what concord hath Mashiach with Belial? or what part hath he that believeth with an infidel?"}],"8":[{"n":9,"text":"For ye know the grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that, though he was rich, yet for your sakes he became poor, that ye through his poverty might be rich."},{"n":23,"text":"Whether any do enquire of Titus, he is my partner and fellowhelper concerning you: or our brethren be enquired of, they are the messengers of the churches, and the glory of Mashiach."}],"9":[{"n":13,"text":"Whiles by the experiment of this ministration they glorify God for your professed subjection unto the gospel of Mashiach, and for your liberal distribution unto them, and unto all men; "}],"10":[{"n":1,"text":"Now I Paul myself beseech you by the meekness and gentleness of Mashiach, who in presence am base among you, but being absent am bold toward you:"},{"n":5,"text":"Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Mashiach;"},{"n":7,"text":"Do ye look on things after the outward appearance? If any man trust to himself that he is Mashiach’s, let him of himself think this again, that, as he is Mashiach’s, even so are we Mashiach’s."},{"n":14,"text":"For we stretch not ourselves beyond our measure, as though we reached not unto you: for we are come as far as to you also in preaching the gospel of Mashiach:"}],"11":[{"n":2,"text":"For I am jealous over you with godly jealousy: for I have espoused you to one husband, that I may present you as a chaste virgin to Mashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Mashiach."},{"n":4,"text":"For if he that cometh preacheth another YahuShua, whom we have not preached, or if ye receive another spirit, which ye have not received, or another gospel, which ye have not accepted, ye might well bear with him. "},{"n":10,"text":"As the truth of Mashiach is in me, no man shall stop me of this boasting in the regions of Achaia."},{"n":13,"text":"For such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of Mashiach."},{"n":23,"text":"Are they ministers of Mashiach? (I speak as a fool) I am more; in labours more abundant, in stripes above measure, in prisons more frequent, in deaths oft."},{"n":31,"text":"The God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, which is blessed for evermore, knoweth that I lie not."}],"12":[{"n":2,"text":"I knew a man in Mashiach above fourteen years ago, (whether in the body, I cannot tell; or whether out of the body, I cannot tell: God knoweth;) such an one caught up to the third heaven."},{"n":9,"text":"And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Mashiach may rest upon me."},{"n":10,"text":"Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities, in reproaches, in necessities, in persecutions, in distresses for Mashiach’s sake: for when I am weak, then am I strong."},{"n":19,"text":"Again, think ye that we excuse ourselves unto you? we speak before God in Mashiach: but we do all things, dearly beloved, for your edifying."}],"13":[{"n":3,"text":"Since ye seek a proof of Mashiach speaking in me, which to you-ward is not weak, but is mighty in you."},{"n":5,"text":"Examine yourselves, whether ye be in the faith; prove your own selves. Know ye not your own selves, how that YahuShua HaMashiach is in you, except ye be reprobates?"},{"n":14,"text":"The grace of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and the love of God, and the communion of the Holy Ghost, be with you all. Amen.  The second epistle to the Corinthians was written from Philippi, a city of Macedonia, by Titus and Lucas. "}]},
"galatians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle, (not of men, neither by man, but by YahuShua HaMashiach, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead;)"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace be to you and peace from God the Father, and from our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"I marvel that ye are so soon removed from him that called you into the grace of Mashiach unto another gospel:"},{"n":7,"text":"Which is not another; but there be some that trouble you, and would pervert the gospel of Mashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"For do I now persuade men, or God? or do I seek to please men? for if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Mashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"For I neither received it of man, neither was I taught it, but by the revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":22,"text":"And was unknown by face unto the churches of Judea which were in Mashiach:"}],"2":[{"n":4,"text":"And that because of false brethren unawares brought in, who came in privily to spy out our liberty which we have in YahuShua HaMashiach, that they might bring us into bondage:"},{"n":16,"text":"Knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law, but by the faith of YahuShua HaMashiach, even we have believed in YahuShua HaMashiach, that we might be justified by the faith of Mashiach, and not by the works of the law: for by the works of the law shall no flesh be justified."},{"n":17,"text":"But if, while we seek to be justified by Mashiach, we ourselves also are found sinners, is therefore Mashiach the minister of sin? God forbid."},{"n":20,"text":"I am crucified with Mashiach: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Mashiach liveth in me: and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by the faith of the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself for me."},{"n":21,"text":"I do not frustrate the grace of God: for if righteousness come by the law, then Mashiach is dead in vain. "}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"O foolish Galatians, who hath bewitched you, that ye should not obey the truth, before whose eyes YahuShua HaMashiach hath been evidently set forth, crucified among you?"},{"n":13,"text":"Mashiach hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree:"},{"n":14,"text":"That the blessing of Abraham might come on the Gentiles through YahuShua HaMashiach; that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith."},{"n":16,"text":"Now to Abraham and his seed were the promises made. He saith not, And to seeds, as of many; but as of one, And to thy seed, which is Mashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"And this I say, that the covenant, that was confirmed before of God in Mashiach, the law, which was four hundred and thirty years after, cannot disannul, that it should make the promise of none effect."},{"n":22,"text":"But the scripture hath concluded all under sin, that the promise by faith of YahuShua HaMashiach might be given to them that believe."},{"n":24,"text":"Wherefore the law was our schoolmaster to bring us unto Mashiach, that we might be justified by faith."},{"n":26,"text":"For ye are all the children of God by faith in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"For as many of you as have been baptized into Mashiach have put on Mashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither bond nor free, there is neither male nor female: for ye are all one in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":29,"text":"And if ye be Mashiach’s, then are ye Abraham’s seed, and heirs according to the promise. "}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"Wherefore thou art no more a servant, but a son; and if a son, then an heir of God through Mashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"And my temptation which was in my flesh ye despised not, nor rejected; but received me as an angel of God, even as YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":19,"text":"My little children, of whom I travail in birth again until Mashiach be formed in you,"}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Mashiach hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage."},{"n":2,"text":"Behold, I Paul say unto you, that if ye be circumcised, Mashiach shall profit you nothing."},{"n":4,"text":"Mashiach is become of no effect unto you, whosoever of you are justified by the law; ye are fallen from grace."},{"n":6,"text":"For in YahuShua HaMashiach neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love."},{"n":24,"text":"And they that are Mashiach’s have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts."}],"6":[{"n":2,"text":"Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Mashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"As many as desire to make a fair shew in the flesh, they constrain you to be circumcised; only lest they should suffer persecution for the cross of Mashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"But God forbid that I should glory, save in the cross of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, by whom the world is crucified unto me, and I unto the world."},{"n":15,"text":"For in YahuShua HaMashiach neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature."},{"n":17,"text":"From henceforth let no man trouble me: for I bear in my body the marks of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":18,"text":"Brethren, the grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with your spirit. Amen.  Unto the Galatians written from Rome. "}]},
"ephesians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, to the saints which are at Ephesus, and to the faithful in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace be to you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who hath blessed us with all spiritual blessings in heavenly places in Mashiach:"},{"n":5,"text":"Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by YahuShua HaMashiach to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,"},{"n":10,"text":"That in the dispensation of the fulness of times he might gather together in one all things in Mashiach, both which are in heaven, and which are on earth; even in him:"},{"n":12,"text":"That we should be to the praise of his glory, who first trusted in Mashiach."},{"n":15,"text":"Wherefore I also, after I heard of your faith in the Lord YahuShua, and love unto all the saints,"},{"n":17,"text":"That the God of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him:"},{"n":20,"text":"Which he wrought in Mashiach, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places, "}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"Even when we were dead in sins, hath quickened us together with Mashiach, (by grace ye are saved;)"},{"n":6,"text":"And hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in heavenly places in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":7,"text":"That in the ages to come he might shew the exceeding riches of his grace in his kindness toward us through YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"For we are his workmanship, created in YahuShua HaMashiach unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them."},{"n":12,"text":"That at that time ye were without Mashiach, being aliens from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers from the covenants of promise, having no hope, and without God in the world:"},{"n":13,"text":"But now in YahuShua HaMashiach ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by the blood of Mashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"And are built upon the foundation of the apostles and prophets, YahuShua HaMashiach himself being the chief corner stone; "}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"For this cause I Paul, the prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach for you Gentiles,"},{"n":4,"text":"Whereby, when ye read, ye may understand my knowledge in the mystery of Mashiach)"},{"n":6,"text":"That the Gentiles should be fellowheirs, and of the same body, and partakers of his promise in Mashiach by the gospel:"},{"n":8,"text":"Unto me, who am less than the least of all saints, is this grace given, that I should preach among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Mashiach;"},{"n":9,"text":"And to make all men see what is the fellowship of the mystery, which from the beginning of the world hath been hid in God, who created all things by YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":11,"text":"According to the eternal purpose which he purposed in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord:"},{"n":14,"text":"For this cause I bow my knees unto the Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":17,"text":"That Mashiach may dwell in your hearts by faith; that ye, being rooted and grounded in love,"},{"n":19,"text":"And to know the love of Mashiach, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of God."},{"n":21,"text":"Unto him be glory in the church by YahuShua HaMashiach throughout all ages, world without end. Amen. "}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"But unto every one of us is given grace according to the measure of the gift of Mashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"For the perfecting of the saints, for the work of the ministry, for the edifying of the body of Mashiach:"},{"n":13,"text":"Till we all come in the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of the Son of God, unto a perfect man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of Mashiach:"},{"n":15,"text":"But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Mashiach:"},{"n":20,"text":"But ye have not so learned Mashiach;"},{"n":21,"text":"If so be that ye have heard him, and have been taught by him, as the truth is in YahuShua:"},{"n":32,"text":"And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Mashiach’s sake hath forgiven you. "}],"5":[{"n":2,"text":"And walk in love, as Mashiach also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweetsmelling savour."},{"n":5,"text":"For this ye know, that no whoremonger, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Mashiach and of God."},{"n":14,"text":"Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Mashiach shall give thee light."},{"n":20,"text":"Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":23,"text":"For the husband is the head of the wife, even as Mashiach is the head of the church: and he is the saviour of the body."},{"n":24,"text":"Therefore as the church is subject unto Mashiach, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing."},{"n":25,"text":"Husbands, love your wives, even as Mashiach also loved the church, and gave himself for it;"},{"n":32,"text":"This is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Mashiach and the church."}],"6":[{"n":5,"text":"Servants, be obedient to them that are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto Mashiach;"},{"n":6,"text":"Not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but as the servants of Mashiach, doing the will of God from the heart;"},{"n":23,"text":"Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":24,"text":"Grace be with all them that love our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach in sincerity. Amen.  Written from Rome unto the Ephesians by Tychicus. "}]},
"philippians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul and Timotheus, the servants of YahuShua HaMashiach, to all the saints in YahuShua HaMashiach which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":8,"text":"For God is my record, how greatly I long after you all in the bowels of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"That ye may approve things that are excellent; that ye may be sincere and without offence till the day of Mashiach;"},{"n":11,"text":"Being filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are by YahuShua HaMashiach, unto the glory and praise of God."},{"n":13,"text":"So that my bonds in Mashiach are manifest in all the palace, and in all other places; "},{"n":15,"text":"Some indeed preach Mashiach even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:"},{"n":16,"text":"The one preach Mashiach of contention, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to my bonds:"},{"n":18,"text":"What then? notwithstanding, every way, whether in pretence, or in truth, Mashiach is preached; and I therein do rejoice, yea, and will rejoice."},{"n":19,"text":"For I know that this shall turn to my salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":20,"text":"According to my earnest expectation and my hope, that in nothing I shall be ashamed, but that with all boldness, as always, so now also Mashiach shall be magnified in my body, whether it be by life, or by death."},{"n":21,"text":"For to me to live is Mashiach, and to die is gain."},{"n":23,"text":"For I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Mashiach; which is far better:"},{"n":26,"text":"That your rejoicing may be more abundant in YahuShua HaMashiach for me by my coming to you again."},{"n":27,"text":"Only let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of Mashiach: that whether I come and see you, or else be absent, I may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;"},{"n":29,"text":"For unto you it is given in the behalf of Mashiach, not only to believe on him, but also to suffer for his sake;"}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"If there be therefore any consolation in Mashiach, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any bowels and mercies,"},{"n":5,"text":"Let this mind be in you, which was also in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":10,"text":"That at the name of YahuShua every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth;"},{"n":11,"text":"And that every tongue should confess that YahuShua HaMashiach is Lord, to the glory of God the Father."},{"n":16,"text":"Holding forth the word of life; that I may rejoice in the day of Mashiach, that I have not run in vain, neither laboured in vain."},{"n":19,"text":"But I trust in the Lord YahuShua to send Timotheus shortly unto you, that I also may be of good comfort, when I know your state."},{"n":21,"text":"For all seek their own, not the things which are YahuShua HaMashiach’s."},{"n":30,"text":"Because for the work of Mashiach he was nigh unto death, not regarding his life, to supply your lack of service toward me. "}],"3":[{"n":3,"text":"For we are the circumcision, which worship God in the spirit, and rejoice in YahuShua HaMashiach, and have no confidence in the flesh."},{"n":7,"text":"But what things were gain to me, those I counted loss for Mashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Yea doubtless, and I count all things but loss for the excellency of the knowledge of YahuShua HaMashiach my Lord: for whom I have suffered the loss of all things, and do count them but dung, that I may win Mashiach,"},{"n":9,"text":"And be found in him, not having mine own righteousness, which is of the law, but that which is through the faith of Mashiach, the righteousness which is of God by faith:"},{"n":12,"text":"Not as though I had already attained, either were already perfect: but I follow after, if that I may apprehend that for which also I am apprehended of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":18,"text":"(For many walk, of whom I have told you often, and now tell you even weeping, that they are the enemies of the cross of Mashiach:"},{"n":20,"text":"For our conversation is in heaven; from whence also we look for the Saviour, the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":13,"text":"I can do all things through Mashiach which strengtheneth me."},{"n":19,"text":"But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"Salute every saint in YahuShua HaMashiach. The brethren which are with me greet you."},{"n":23,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen.  It was written to the Philippians from Rome by Epaphroditus. "}]},
"colossians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, and Timotheus our brother,"},{"n":2,"text":"To the saints and faithful brethren in Mashiach which are at Colosse: Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"We give thanks to God and the Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, praying always for you,"},{"n":4,"text":"Since we heard of your faith in YahuShua HaMashiach, and of the love which ye have to all the saints,"},{"n":7,"text":"As ye also learned of Epaphras our dear fellowservant, who is for you a faithful minister of Mashiach;"},{"n":24,"text":"Who now rejoice in my sufferings for you, and fill up that which is behind of the afflictions of Mashiach in my flesh for his body’s sake, which is the church:"},{"n":27,"text":"To whom God would make known what is the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles; which is Mashiach in you, the hope of glory:"},{"n":28,"text":"Whom we preach, warning every man, and teaching every man in all wisdom; that we may present every man perfect in YahuShua HaMashiach:"}],"2":[{"n":2,"text":"That their hearts might be comforted, being knit together in love, and unto all riches of the full assurance of understanding, to the acknowledgement of the mystery of God, and of the Father, and of Mashiach;"},{"n":5,"text":"For though I be absent in the flesh, yet am I with you in the spirit, joying and beholding your order, and the stedfastness of your faith in Mashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"As ye have therefore received YahuShua HaMashiach the Lord, so walk ye in him:"},{"n":8,"text":"Beware lest any man spoil you through philosophy and vain deceit, after the tradition of men, after the rudiments of the world, and not after Mashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"In whom also ye are circumcised with the circumcision made without hands, in putting off the body of the sins of the flesh by the circumcision of Mashiach:"},{"n":17,"text":"Which are a shadow of things to come; but the body is of Mashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"Wherefore if ye be dead with Mashiach from the rudiments of the world, why, as though living in the world, are ye subject to ordinances,"}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"If ye then be risen with Mashiach, seek those things which are above, where Mashiach sitteth on the right hand of God."},{"n":3,"text":"For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Mashiach in God."},{"n":4,"text":"When Mashiach, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory."},{"n":11,"text":"Where there is neither Greek nor Jew, circumcision nor uncircumcision, Barbarian, Scythian, bond nor free: but Mashiach is all, and in all."},{"n":13,"text":"Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Mashiach forgave you, so also do ye."},{"n":16,"text":"Let the word of Mashiach dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord."},{"n":17,"text":"And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord YahuShua, giving thanks to God and the Father by him."},{"n":24,"text":"Knowing that of the Lord ye shall receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve the Lord Mashiach."}],"4":[{"n":3,"text":"Withal praying also for us, that God would open unto us a door of utterance, to speak the mystery of Mashiach, for which I am also in bonds:"},{"n":12,"text":"Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of Mashiach, saluteth you, always labouring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God."}]},
"1thessalonians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus, unto the church of the Thessalonians which is in God the Father and in the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach: Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Remembering without ceasing your work of faith, and labour of love, and patience of hope in our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, in the sight of God and our Father;"},{"n":10,"text":"And to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, even YahuShua, which delivered us from the wrath to come. "}],"2":[{"n":6,"text":"Nor of men sought we glory, neither of you, nor yet of others, when we might have been burdensome, as the apostles of Mashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"For ye, brethren, became followers of the churches of God which in Judea are in YahuShua HaMashiach: for ye also have suffered like things of your own countrymen, even as they have of the Jews:"},{"n":15,"text":"Who both killed the Lord YahuShua, and their own prophets, and have persecuted us; and they please not God, and are contrary to all men:"},{"n":19,"text":"For what is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing? Are not even ye in the presence of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach at his coming?"}],"3":[{"n":2,"text":"And sent Timotheus, our brother, and minister of God, and our fellowlabourer in the gospel of Mashiach, to establish you, and to comfort you concerning your faith:"},{"n":11,"text":"Now God himself and our Father, and our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, direct our way unto you."},{"n":13,"text":"To the end he may stablish your hearts unblameable in holiness before God, even our Father, at the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach with all his saints. "}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Furthermore then we beseech you, brethren, and exhort you by the Lord YahuShua, that as ye have received of us how ye ought to walk and to please God, so ye would abound more and more."},{"n":2,"text":"For ye know what commandments we gave you by the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":14,"text":"For if we believe that YahuShua died and rose again, even so them also which sleep in YahuShua will God bring with him."},{"n":16,"text":"For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Mashiach shall rise first:"}],"5":[{"n":9,"text":"For God hath not appointed us to wrath, but to obtain salvation by our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":18,"text":"In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in YahuShua HaMashiach concerning you."},{"n":23,"text":"And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you. Amen.  The first epistle unto the Thessalonians was written from Athens. "}]},
"2thessalonians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus, unto the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace unto you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"And to you who are troubled rest with us, when the Lord YahuShua shall be revealed from heaven with his mighty angels,"},{"n":8,"text":"In flaming fire taking vengeance on them that know not God, and that obey not the gospel of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":12,"text":"That the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach may be glorified in you, and ye in him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach. "}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Now we beseech you, brethren, by the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and by our gathering together unto him,"},{"n":2,"text":"That ye be not soon shaken in mind, or be troubled, neither by spirit, nor by word, nor by letter as from us, as that the day of Mashiach is at hand."},{"n":14,"text":"Whereunto he called you by our gospel, to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":16,"text":"Now our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach himself, and God, even our Father, which hath loved us, and hath given us everlasting consolation and good hope through grace,"}],"3":[{"n":5,"text":"And the Lord direct your hearts into the love of God, and into the patient waiting for Mashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"Now we command you, brethren, in the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that ye withdraw yourselves from every brother that walketh disorderly, and not after the tradition which he received of us."},{"n":12,"text":"Now them that are such we command and exhort by our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that with quietness they work, and eat their own bread."},{"n":18,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen.  The second epistle to the Thessalonians was written from Athens. "}]},
"1timothy":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the commandment of God our Saviour, and Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, which is our hope;"},{"n":2,"text":"Unto Timothy, my own son in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God our Father and YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":12,"text":"And I thank YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, who hath enabled me, for that he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry;"},{"n":14,"text":"And the grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant with faith and love which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":15,"text":"This is a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that YahuShua HaMashiach came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief."},{"n":16,"text":"Howbeit for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first YahuShua HaMashiach might shew forth all longsuffering, for a pattern to them which should hereafter believe on him to life everlasting."}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":7,"text":"Whereunto I am ordained a preacher, and an apostle, (I speak the truth in Mashiach, and lie not;) a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and verity."}],"3":[{"n":13,"text":"For they that have used the office of a deacon well purchase to themselves a good degree, and great boldness in the faith which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":6,"text":"If thou put the brethren in remembrance of these things, thou shalt be a good minister of YahuShua HaMashiach, nourished up in the words of faith and of good doctrine, whereunto thou hast attained."}],"5":[{"n":11,"text":"But the younger widows refuse: for when they have begun to wax wanton against Mashiach, they will marry;"},{"n":21,"text":"I charge thee before God, and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and the elect angels, that thou observe these things without preferring one before another, doing nothing by partiality."}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"If any man teach otherwise, and consent not to wholesome words, even the words of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and to the doctrine which is according to godliness;"},{"n":13,"text":"I give thee charge in the sight of God, who quickeneth all things, and before YahuShua HaMashiach, who before Pontius Pilate witnessed a good confession;"},{"n":14,"text":"That thou keep this commandment without spot, unrebukeable, until the appearing of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"}]},
"2timothy":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, according to the promise of life which is in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":2,"text":"To Timothy, my dearly beloved son: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":9,"text":"Who hath saved us, and called us with an holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in YahuShua HaMashiach before the world began,"},{"n":10,"text":"But is now made manifest by the appearing of our Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach, who hath abolished death, and hath brought life and immortality to light through the gospel:"},{"n":13,"text":"Hold fast the form of sound words, which thou hast heard of me, in faith and love which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Thou therefore, my son, be strong in the grace that is in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Thou therefore endure hardness, as a good soldier of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Remember that YahuShua HaMashiach of the seed of David was raised from the dead according to my gospel:"},{"n":10,"text":"Therefore I endure all things for the elect’s sakes, that they may also obtain the salvation which is in YahuShua HaMashiach with eternal glory."},{"n":19,"text":"Nevertheless the foundation of God standeth sure, having this seal, The Lord knoweth them that are his. And, Let every one that nameth the name of Mashiach depart from iniquity."}],"3":[{"n":12,"text":"Yea, and all that will live godly in YahuShua HaMashiach shall suffer persecution."},{"n":15,"text":"And that from a child thou hast known the holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"I charge thee therefore before God, and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who shall judge the quick and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom;"},{"n":22,"text":"The Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with thy spirit. Grace be with you. Amen.  The second epistle unto Timotheus, ordained the first bishop of the church of the Ephesians, was written from Rome, when Paul was brought before Nero the second time. "}]},
"titus":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;"},{"n":4,"text":"To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach our Saviour."}],"2":[{"n":13,"text":"Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach;"}],"3":[{"n":6,"text":"Which he shed on us abundantly through YahuShua HaMashiach our Saviour;"}]},
"philemon":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":5,"text":"Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord YahuShua, and toward all saints;"},{"n":6,"text":"That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Wherefore, though I might be much bold in Mashiach to enjoin thee that which is convenient,"},{"n":9,"text":"Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":23,"text":"There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":25,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with your spirit. Amen.  Written from Rome to Philemon, by Onesimus a servant. "}]},
"hebrews":{"2":[{"n":9,"text":"But we see YahuShua, who was made a little lower than the angels for the suffering of death, crowned with glory and honour; that he by the grace of God should taste death for every man."}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our profession, YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":6,"text":"But Mashiach as a son over his own house; whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm unto the end."},{"n":14,"text":"For we are made partakers of Mashiach, if we hold the beginning of our confidence stedfast unto the end;"}],"4":[{"n":8,"text":"For if Joshua had given them rest, then would he not afterward have spoken of another day."},{"n":14,"text":"Seeing then that we have a great high priest, that is passed into the heavens, YahuShua the Son of God, let us hold fast our profession."}],"5":[{"n":5,"text":"So also Mashiach glorified not himself to be made an high priest; but he that said unto him, Thou art my Son, to day have I begotten thee."}],"6":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore leaving the principles of the doctrine of Mashiach, let us go on unto perfection; not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith toward God,"},{"n":20,"text":"Whither the forerunner is for us entered, even YahuShua, made an high priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec. "}],"7":[{"n":22,"text":"By so much was YahuShua made a surety of a better testament."}],"9":[{"n":11,"text":"But Mashiach being come an high priest of good things to come, by a greater and more perfect tabernacle, not made with hands, that is to say, not of this building;"},{"n":14,"text":"How much more shall the blood of Mashiach, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without spot to God, purge your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?"},{"n":24,"text":"For Mashiach is not entered into the holy places made with hands, which are the figures of the true; but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God for us:"},{"n":28,"text":"So Mashiach was once offered to bear the sins of many; and unto them that look for him shall he appear the second time without sin unto salvation. "}],"10":[{"n":10,"text":"By the which will we are sanctified through the offering of the body of YahuShua HaMashiach once for all. "},{"n":19,"text":"Having therefore, brethren, boldness to enter into the holiest by the blood of YahuShua,"}],"11":[{"n":26,"text":"Esteeming the reproach of Mashiach greater riches than the treasures in Egypt: for he had respect unto the recompence of the reward."}],"12":[{"n":2,"text":"Looking unto YahuShua the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God."},{"n":24,"text":"And to YahuShua the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel."}],"13":[{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua HaMashiach the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever."},{"n":12,"text":"Wherefore YahuShua also, that he might sanctify the people with his own blood, suffered without the gate."},{"n":20,"text":"Now the God of peace, that brought again from the dead our Lord YahuShua, that great shepherd of the sheep, through the blood of the everlasting covenant,"},{"n":21,"text":"Make you perfect in every good work to do his will, working in you that which is wellpleasing in his sight, through YahuShua HaMashiach; to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen."}]},
"james":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"James, a servant of God and of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"My brethren, have not the faith of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Lord of glory, with respect of persons."}]},
"1peter":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Peter, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, to the strangers scattered throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,"},{"n":2,"text":"Elect according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, through sanctification of the Spirit, unto obedience and sprinkling of the blood of YahuShua HaMashiach: Grace unto you, and peace, be multiplied."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, which according to his abundant mercy hath begotten us again unto a lively hope by the resurrection of YahuShua HaMashiach from the dead,"},{"n":7,"text":"That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":11,"text":"Searching what, or what manner of time the Spirit of Mashiach which was in them did signify, when it testified beforehand the sufferings of Mashiach, and the glory that should follow."},{"n":13,"text":"Wherefore gird up the loins of your mind, be sober, and hope to the end for the grace that is to be brought unto you at the revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":19,"text":"But with the precious blood of Mashiach, as of a lamb without blemish and without spot:"}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"Ye also, as lively stones, are built up a spiritual house, an holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God by YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"For even hereunto were ye called: because Mashiach also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps:"}],"3":[{"n":16,"text":"Having a good conscience; that, whereas they speak evil of you, as of evildoers, they may be ashamed that falsely accuse your good conversation in Mashiach."},{"n":18,"text":"For Mashiach also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:"},{"n":21,"text":"The like figure whereunto even baptism doth also now save us (not the putting away of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God,) by the resurrection of YahuShua HaMashiach:"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Forasmuch then as Mashiach hath suffered for us in the flesh, arm yourselves likewise with the same mind: for he that hath suffered in the flesh hath ceased from sin;"},{"n":11,"text":"If any man speak, let him speak as the oracles of God; if any man minister, let him do it as of the ability which God giveth: that God in all things may be glorified through YahuShua HaMashiach, to whom be praise and dominion for ever and ever. Amen."},{"n":13,"text":"But rejoice, inasmuch as ye are partakers of Mashiach’s sufferings; that, when his glory shall be revealed, ye may be glad also with exceeding joy."},{"n":14,"text":"If ye be reproached for the name of Mashiach, happy are ye; for the spirit of glory and of God resteth upon you: on their part he is evil spoken of, but on your part he is glorified."}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"The elders which are among you I exhort, who am also an elder, and a witness of the sufferings of Mashiach, and also a partaker of the glory that shall be revealed:"},{"n":10,"text":"But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by YahuShua HaMashiach, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you."},{"n":14,"text":"Greet ye one another with a kiss of charity. Peace be with you all that are in YahuShua HaMashiach. Amen.  "}]},
"2peter":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Simon Peter, a servant and an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, to them that have obtained like precious faith with us through the righteousness of God and our Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace and peace be multiplied unto you through the knowledge of God, and of YahuShua our Lord,"},{"n":8,"text":"For if these things be in you, and abound, they make you that ye shall neither be barren nor unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"For so an entrance shall be ministered unto you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"Knowing that shortly I must put off this my tabernacle, even as our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach hath shewed me."},{"n":16,"text":"For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty."}],"2":[{"n":20,"text":"For if after they have escaped the pollutions of the world through the knowledge of the Lord and Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach, they are again entangled therein, and overcome, the latter end is worse with them than the beginning."}],"3":[{"n":18,"text":"But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour YahuShua HaMashiach. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.  "}]},
"1john":{"1":[{"n":3,"text":"That which we have seen and heard declare we unto you, that ye also may have fellowship with us: and truly our fellowship is with the Father, and with his Son YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of YahuShua HaMashiach his Son cleanseth us from all sin."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, YahuShua HaMashiach the righteous:"},{"n":22,"text":"Who is a liar but he that denieth that YahuShua is HaMashiach? He is antichrist, that denieth the Father and the Son."}],"3":[{"n":23,"text":"And this is his commandment, That we should believe on the name of his Son YahuShua HaMashiach, and love one another, as he gave us commandment."}],"4":[{"n":2,"text":"Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that YahuShua HaMashiach is come in the flesh is of God:"},{"n":3,"text":"And every spirit that confesseth not that YahuShua HaMashiach is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world."},{"n":15,"text":"Whosoever shall confess that YahuShua is the Son of God, God dwelleth in him, and he in God."}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Whosoever believeth that YahuShua is HaMashiach is born of God: and every one that loveth him that begat loveth him also that is begotten of him."},{"n":5,"text":"Who is he that overcometh the world, but he that believeth that YahuShua is the Son of God?"},{"n":6,"text":"This is he that came by water and blood, even YahuShua HaMashiach; not by water only, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit that beareth witness, because the Spirit is truth."},{"n":20,"text":"And we know that the Son of God is come, and hath given us an understanding, that we may know him that is true, and we are in him that is true, even in his Son YahuShua HaMashiach. This is the true God, and eternal life."}]},
"2john":{"1":[{"n":3,"text":"Grace be with you, mercy, and peace, from God the Father, and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Son of the Father, in truth and love."},{"n":7,"text":"For many deceivers are entered into the world, who confess not that YahuShua HaMashiach is come in the flesh. This is a deceiver and an antichrist."},{"n":9,"text":"Whosoever transgresseth, and abideth not in the doctrine of Mashiach, hath not God. He that abideth in the doctrine of Mashiach, he hath both the Father and the Son."}]},
"jude":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Jude, the servant of YahuShua HaMashiach, and brother of James, to them that are sanctified by God the Father, and preserved in YahuShua HaMashiach, and called:"},{"n":4,"text":"For there are certain men crept in unawares, who were before of old ordained to this condemnation, ungodly men, turning the grace of our God into lasciviousness, and denying the only Lord God, and our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"But, beloved, remember ye the words which were spoken before of the apostles of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":21,"text":"Keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach unto eternal life."}]},
"revelation":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The Revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach, which God gave unto him, to shew unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass; and he sent and signified it by his angel unto his servant John:"},{"n":2,"text":"Who bare record of the word of God, and of the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach, and of all things that he saw."},{"n":5,"text":"And from YahuShua HaMashiach, who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth. Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his own blood,"},{"n":9,"text":"I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of YahuShua HaMashiach, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"11":[{"n":15,"text":"And the seventh angel sounded; and there were great voices in heaven, saying, The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Mashiach; and he shall reign for ever and ever."}],"12":[{"n":10,"text":"And I heard a loud voice saying in heaven, Now is come salvation, and strength, and the kingdom of our God, and the power of his Mashiach: for the accuser of our brethren is cast down, which accused them before our God day and night."},{"n":17,"text":"And the dragon was wroth with the woman, and went to make war with the remnant of her seed, which keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach. "}],"14":[{"n":12,"text":"Here is the patience of the saints: here are they that keep the commandments of God, and the faith of YahuShua."}],"17":[{"n":6,"text":"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of YahuShua: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration."}],"19":[{"n":10,"text":"And I fell at his feet to worship him. And he said unto me, See thou do it not: I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren that have the testimony of YahuShua: worship God: for the testimony of YahuShua is the spirit of prophecy."}],"20":[{"n":4,"text":"And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of YahuShua, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Mashiach a thousand years."},{"n":6,"text":"Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Mashiach, and shall reign with him a thousand years."}],"22":[{"n":16,"text":"I YahuShua have sent mine angel to testify unto you these things in the churches. I am the root and the offspring of David, and the bright and morning star."},{"n":20,"text":"He which testifieth these things saith, Surely I come quickly. Amen. Even so, come, Lord YahuShua."},{"n":21,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen.   "}]}
};
